window.receiveProjectSource({"path": ".docs/specs/ingest/DESIGN-media-processing.md", "lines": ["# Design \u2014 Media Processing & Storage (images / audio / video)", "", "| | |", "|---|---|", "| **Type** | Workstream scoping design \u2014 DATA-4 (multi-modal adapters + media extraction/storage) |", "| **Status** | In progress \u2014 image (\u00a75), audio (\u00a76), video (\u00a77) pipeline chunks authored 2026-07-20; **storage & clip policy (\u00a79, M-3) + GovCloud serving (\u00a710) chunks authored 2026-07-21**; forks M-4\u2013M-7 resolved 2026-07-20; M-1 eval designed, execution open (chunk plan \u00a78); pass-3 fold-down complete 2026-07-21 \u2014 slot identity + canonical locators (\u00a75.3/\u00a76.2), member-mapping supersession (\u00a75.3\u2013\u00a75.5), observation/event carrier precision (\u00a75.4/\u00a76.3), child-object identity (\u00a77.2), union read contract (\u00a77.6), M-5 scope fix (\u00a76.3); **pass-4 review (2026-07-21, `codex-review-pass4.md`) folded** \u2014 clip coalescing epoch, child-evidence catalog + destruction lifecycle, stream-copy wording, evidence-level corrections in \u00a710, air-gap posture; **long-running/live-stream extension (\u00a77.7) authored 2026-07-26; Claude Opus 5 adversarial corrections triaged/folded 2026-07-27** \u2014 finite chunk identity, stream epochs, layered windows, cross-chunk state/promotion/clips, optional operation binding, posture-specific overload, control-shard admission, bounded late correction, capture-time coverage, and lifecycle closure |", "| **Program** | Government Intelligence-Layer Program \u2014 authoritative state in `STATE.md` (this dir) |", "| **Relation** | Feeds artifact shapes (frame metadata, transcripts, detections, clips) into the ingestion design's persistence + field-provenance model (`DESIGN-data-ingestion.md` \u00a73.5). Media artifacts ride the same write contract \u2014 **consumed by the now-authored ingestion extraction & persistence chunk (ingestion \u00a74.2\u2013\u00a74.6, 2026-07-21)** |", "| **Live-stream phasing** | \u00a77.7 is design-ready but deferred/need-triggered; no continuous-stream adapter/runtime is an automatic V1 build |", "", "## 1. Scope & why now", "", "Finite image/prerecorded-video ingestion and extraction are Phase-1 scope (program 2026-07-14; BRD FR-3.6);", "continuous/live video is the deferred \u00a77.7 extension. Audio joins here because video's audio track requires", "it anyway. This doc owns *how* non-text modalities are processed", "(models, tracks, context-conditioning) and *stored* (clips, transcripts, detections, provenance). It is", "**not** a V1-slice item (`DESIGN-data-ingestion.md` \u00a71.2); its artifact shapes predate and are consumed by", "the ingestion extraction & persistence chunk (ingestion \u00a74.2\u2013\u00a74.6, authored 2026-07-21). In particular,", "\u00a77.7's continuous/live-stream capability is **design-ready but deferred**: \u201cauthored\u201d/\u201cDONE\u201d in this", "document means the contract is ready for estimation and review, not that it belongs to the automatic V1", "build.", "", "## 2. Settled inputs (program decisions \u2014 do not re-decide)", "", "- **Deterministic frame sampling is the committed video-visual baseline**; hosted vision models", "  commercially; Nova-class or self-hosted in-VPC vision in GovCloud (STATE 2026-07-14).", "- **In-VPC/self-hosted CV/GPU at firehose scale** \u2014 Bedrock per-frame cost/quotas cannot carry the extreme", "  tier (STATE 2026-07-14 video-volume refinement). Must-verify: GovCloud GPU capacity/quotas.", "- **External-reference posture for raw video**: a scheme-valid versioned locator + available content hash into the customer's archive; short **evidence", "  clips** around detections are the retained evidence; clip policy is per-source-type **with customer", "  sign-off** and is the dominant retained volume (STATE 2026-07-14; BRD FR-4.2/4.4).", "- **Context-conditioned extraction**: the per-source onboarding config (DATA-12) supplies context \u2014", "  \"satellite imagery of X,\" \"CCTV of Y,\" \"body-cam of Z\" \u2014 which sets the extraction target set (satellite \u2192", "  objects/changes; CCTV frame \u2192 people/vehicles).", "- **Audio requirement (product owner, via 2026-07-18 handoff \u00a75.C):** the transcript is **more than", "  speech-to-text** \u2014 (a) diarized speech\u2192text where possible, (b) **non-language audio description**", "  (gunshot, glass break, vehicle, alarm) to the closed-caption-for-the-deaf standard; these sounds carry", "  investigative signal.", "- **Persistence is not re-decided here**: media payloads/evidence follow ingestion \u00a73.0's disposition and", "  acquisition contract. An `external_reference` means the original bytes were not held at acceptance; a later", "  permitted fetch may be transient or durable and is recorded separately. Extracted artifacts are canonical", "  SoR rows + hot projections carrying field-level provenance + labels (ingestion \u00a73.5).", "- **GovCloud vision**: Nova Micro/Lite/Pro are in-region us-gov-west-1 (Nova Pro takes video \u22641 GB via S3", "  URI), but **Nova is NOT FedRAMP-authorized \u2014 verified 2026-07-20, re-verified 2026-07-21** against AWS's", "  Bedrock-models certification page (page last updated 2026-07-14; no Nova entry). Native-video in-boundary", "  stays **gated on authorization** \u2014 a watch item, not a promise. Same page, **exact dated allowlist", "  (re-verified 2026-07-21, pass-4 \u2014 replaces family-range prose):** the GovCloud (FedRAMP) column lists", "  Claude 3 Haiku, 3.5 Haiku, 3.5 Sonnet v1/v2, 3.7 Sonnet, 4.0 Sonnet, 4.1 Opus, 4.5 Haiku, 4.5 Sonnet,", "  4.5 Opus, **4.6 Sonnet, 4.6 Opus**. **IL4/5 was NOT confirmed on the 2026-07-21 read** (no DoD CSP SRG", "  marks visible on the models table \u2014 re-verify; material only under a DoD flow-down, ENV-2). An", "  *authorized* hosted-VLM **frame** path is therefore a **candidate**, not a selected serving path, until", "  the in-account checks pass: image input enabled on GovCloud endpoints + the effective model-access set", "  (\u00a77.4, \u00a710.5 items 1\u20132).", "", "## 3. Processing model per modality (to be authored in chunks)", "", "**The processing shape is a funnel, not a model pick** (the settled funnel principle + in-VPC CV decision", "applied to media): **Tier 0** \u2014 near-free deterministic reduction (scene/motion segmentation, keyframe", "extraction; CPU) cuts raw footage to its active segments \u2014 on surveillance video this alone often drops the", "bulk of the material before any model spends anything; **Tier 1** \u2014 cheap deterministic CV (in-VPC", "detection/tracking: persons / vehicles / plates) over sampled frames of active segments, producing the", "structured detections + timestamps that drive evidence clips; **Tier 2** \u2014 premium models spent selectively:", "VLM description/OCR on Tier-1-flagged frames, and native-video calls on short high-value segments where", "temporal narrative matters (per M-1) \u2014 never the whole file. The audio track runs in parallel. The mix is", "context-dependent (body-cam \u2248 always active; CCTV \u2248 mostly empty) and set by the per-source config", "(DATA-12). Best data per dollar comes from the mix; the M-1 eval quantifies it.", "", "- **Images** \u2192 vision extraction: entities (person / vehicle / plate / location), object/scene detections,", "  OCR of text-in-image, timestamps. Context drives the target set. **Specified in \u00a75.**", "- **Audio** \u2192 one time-coded transcript pipeline: diarized speech + non-speech event description (M-2", "  resolved \u2192 A). **Specified in \u00a76.**", "- **Video** \u2192 **dual-track**: (a) visual \u2014 deterministic frame sampling into the image pipeline (baseline);", "  native-video-model as an evaluated per-source option (fork M-1); (b) audio track \u2192 the audio pipeline.", "  **Specified in \u00a77.**", "- **CXOS contexts** (what the footage actually is): surveillance/CCTV canvass, body-cam, evidence", "  photos/video \u2192 extraction targets people/vehicles/plates/locations/times \u2192 tenant-scoped entities + events", "  + relationship edges, all via the ingestion write contract. Immutable observations may accrue onto a", "  scoped identity such as \"the white truck\" inside the permitted client-standing or operation universe;", "  speculative identity candidates/scores remain DataLake2 state, and accepted links publish to Accelerate.", "", "## 4. Open forks & verify items", "", "- **M-1 \u2014 Native video model: evaluate the *mix*, don't commit \u2014 CONFIRMED 2026-07-19.** Nova Pro does take", "  video natively (\u22641 GB via S3 URI, in-region us-gov-west-1 \u2014 STATE Bedrock findings 2026-07-10; FedRAMP:", "  **verified NOT authorized as of 2026-07-20** \u2014 \u00a72). Frame sampling stays the only committed path. The eval question, sharpened by", "  the product owner's \"best data for the money\" framing: **for a fixed budget per hour of footage, which \u00a73", "  tier mix yields the most useful extractions** \u2014 dense frames to a VLM, sparse frames + CV triage,", "  native-video on active segments, hybrids \u2014 scored on temporal reasoning, cost/hour, determinism/", "  reproducibility, and evidence quality. **Eval design authored 2026-07-20 (\u00a77.4); the former verify-items", "  are verified** \u2014 Nova video caps + commercial pricing confirmed from AWS docs, and Nova is confirmed", "  **absent** from the Bedrock FedRAMP certification page (2026-07-14 page update), so the native-video arm", "  is commercial-only until authorization lands (\u00a72, \u00a77.4). Execution of the eval remains open (gated on a", "  ground-truth footage corpus \u2014 \u00a77.4 inputs).", "- **M-2 \u2014 Transcript artifact modeling \u2014 RESOLVED 2026-07-19 \u2192 A.** One **time-coded transcript artifact**", "  per audio source: diarized speech + non-speech sound descriptions inline, caption-style, one timeline.", "  Investigatively-significant detections are **additionally promoted to events** per source config, each", "  event's provenance referencing its transcript segment (ingestion \u00a73.5 contribution rows), so the", "  derivation is unambiguous. **Design principle (product owner): timelines are assembled at write time \u2014", "  never left for an AI consumer to zip together in context** (a model handed two parallel streams cannot", "  reliably reconstruct sequence). Why B (split artifacts) never pulls its weight here: A's event promotion", "  *already provides* the independent detection stream B offers; a speech-free acoustic feed is a transcript", "  whose lines are all non-speech (or an events-only source by config); and speech/acoustic models running at", "  different cadences is an assembly detail behind the write (late outputs = a new artifact version), not an", "  artifact-model fork. **Scope clarification (product owner, 2026-07-20, recorded with the M-7", "  resolution):** the write-time-assembly principle is scoped to **intra-artifact modeling** (one", "  transcript, not split audio artifacts); it does not mandate stored timeline rows \u2014 its", "  never-zip-in-context half is a platform **read guarantee** (see M-7).", "- **M-3 \u2014 Evidence-clip policy defaults \u2014 AUTHORED 2026-07-21 (\u00a79).** Config, not architecture, as flagged:", "  clip mechanics + context-class default seeds (\u00a79.2, \u00a79.5), retained-volume model (\u00a79.4), reference", "  validation (\u00a79.3), sign-off flow (\u00a79.5). Two postures pinned in the authoring (engineering within the", "  recorded evidence posture, flagged to the product owner in-session): clips are **stream copies \u2014 no", "  elementary-stream re-encoding** \u2014 cut at keyframe boundaries and remuxed, with the derivation fully", "  recorded (requested window \u2286 recorded actual range; custody claims provable derivation, never byte", "  identity \u2014 pass-4 wording; display transcodes are downstream display objects, never the evidence), and", "  **retention duration has no platform default** \u2014", "  it is a required, fail-closed customer sign-off value per byte class.", "- **M-4 \u2014 Detection/OCR artifact granularity \u2014 RESOLVED 2026-07-20 \u2192 A** (product owner; dated STATE", "  entry). One `image_analysis` artifact per analyzed image, member-keyed collections. Owner rationale:", "  everything found in an image must tie back to the image's artifact row \u2014 A gives that by construction", "  (findings live *inside* the row as members; anything promoted out points back at its exact member path", "  via \u00a73.5 contribution rows). The \"what counts as a detection\" definition is in \u00a75.3. **Refinement", "  2026-07-21 (product owner, resolving the pass-3 empty-analysis finding):** artifacts are per analyzed", "  image *with findings*; per-frame execution coverage including empty results is ledger-manifest ground truth,", "  while agent-facing source-item coverage and any registry-promised frame-level negative evidence publish to", "  Accelerate before hot projection (publication-boundary amendment 2026-09-11). Per-source threshold pairs", "  (record floor < report threshold) shrink the true-empty class (STATE 2026-07-21). Options kept below for the record. \u2014 Original framing: what is", "  a *row* in the", "  system of record when one analyzed image yields N detections + M OCR blocks? The ingestion \u00a73.5 contract", "  permits either shape (collections address members by stable key). Grounding for the scoring: the SoR must", "  stay the narrowest stream in the pipeline (ingestion \u00a74.1 write-load posture) and is never the analytics", "  target (ingestion \u00a73.1) \u2014 the hot projection, not the canonical row shape, serves per-detection queries.", "  - **(A) One `image_analysis` artifact per analyzed image; detections/OCR blocks as member-keyed collection", "    fields \u2014 8/10, recommended.** Pros: SoR rows scale with images-with-findings, not detections (a single", "    camera's frame stream would otherwise mint the platform's largest table); one fail-closed transaction", "    per image (\u00a73.5); mirrors the resolved M-2 transcript shape (segments as members) \u2014 one addressing", "    pattern across media; significant detections already become first-class rows *via promotion* (events,", "    entity observations), so importance surfaces as rows without defaulting everything to rows; the hot", "    projection can flatten members into per-detection rows if the query mix wants it (a projection concern,", "    not SoR schema). Cons: per-detection queries against the SoR itself walk JSONB members (acceptable under", "    the \u00a73.1 invariant); no per-detection supersession (versioning stays artifact-grain, as \u00a73.5 has it", "    everywhere).", "  - **(B) Every detection its own artifact row \u2014 3/10.** Pros: hot-store rows with no flattening step;", "    per-detection versioning. Cons: row explosion in the SoR at frame-stream scale \u2014 directly against the", "    narrowest-stream posture, and would make detections the first artifact type forced into the born-in-hot", "    escape hatch; transaction fan-out per image; a second addressing pattern beside the transcript's.", "  - **(C) One artifact per processing batch/segment (N frames) \u2014 5/10.** Pros: fewest rows; matches how", "    video Tier-1 actually batches work. Cons: two-level member addressing (segment \u2192 frame \u2192 detection)", "    makes evidence display and Tier-4 presentation harder; meaningless for standalone images. Best kept as", "    A's *coarsening dial* for firehose video (the same delivery-unit-grain move as ingestion \u00a74.1), decided", "    in the video chunk \u2014 not the default shape.", "- **M-5 \u2014 Entity minting from media detections \u2014 RESOLVED 2026-07-20 \u2192 A** (product owner; dated STATE", "  entry): identity-handle-gated auto-mint; anonymous detections never mint. \u00a75.4 specifies. Options kept", "  below for the record. \u2014 Original framing: the V1 slice mints", "  person/vehicle/location tenant-scoped entities from *structured submission fields*; media detections are mostly", "  anonymous (a person-shaped box, not a person). ENT-1 ground rules apply: false-merge cost is high, merges", "  are human-adjudicated with reversal, and cross-mission linking is never silent (cross-operation", "  visibility is policy-gated \u2014 Apollo STATE D4/Q-25).", "  - **(A) Identity-handle-gated auto-mint \u2014 8/10, recommended.** A detection mints an entity-observation", "    artifact (assertion semantics, \u00a73.5) only when it carries a resolvable identity handle: plate string \u2192", "    vehicle; EXIF/overlay GPS \u2192 location; OCR'd VIN/serial \u2192 vehicle/item; OCR'd *names* ride the text", "    path's existing entity extraction (\u00a75.5), not a media-private one. Anonymous person/vehicle detections", "    stay detections + promoted events \u2014 queryable, clip-linked, no entity row. Pros: captures the", "    deterministic, explainable wins (camera plate \u2194 submitted vehicle joins \u2014 exactly the cross-referencing", "    the funnel exists to feed) with no registry pollution; honest about what CV actually asserts. Cons:", "    \"same unknown person on two cameras\" is not an entity in v1 \u2014 it stays in detections/tracks", "    (re-identification is precisely the unproven capability option B depends on).", "  - **(B) Mint anonymous scoped entities per detection track \u2014 3/10.** Pros: maximal recall; \"unknown person\"", "    as a first-class node from day 1. Cons: floods the registry with unmergeable anonymous entities; their", "    value depends on cross-camera re-identification \u2014 an in-VPC capability we have not evaluated and must", "    not assume; the false-merge risk is the exact ENT-1 warning; adjudication load lands on humans", "    immediately.", "  - **(C) No auto-mint from media; humans mint via review \u2014 4/10.** Pros: zero pollution risk; fits the", "    onboarding dry-run posture. Cons: forfeits the safe deterministic handles (plates, GPS) that carry most", "    of media's cross-referencing value; makes media evidence second-class next to text.", "- **M-6 \u2014 Biometric identification (face / voice) scope \u2014 RESOLVED 2026-07-20 \u2192 A** (product owner; dated", "  STATE entry): v1 non-goal, registered as its own decision gate should a real requirement arrive. Options", "  kept below for the record. \u2014 Original framing: person", "  *detection* (a box, a track) is in scope; person *identification* from biometrics is a different", "  capability with a different risk class, and nothing in the program record requires it.", "  - **(A) v1 non-goal, registered as its own decision gate \u2014 9/10, recommended.** No face or voice identity", "    matching anywhere in the pipeline; diarization speaker labels stay transcript-local (\u00a76.2). If an", "    Apollo/TBI requirement arrives, it opens as its own scoped workstream \u2014 compliance/policy first (CJIS,", "    state-law variance), then capability eval \u2014 not a config flag on this pipeline. Note: biometric match", "    results *produced by customer systems* and delivered inside their records are ordinary fields \u2014 shape", "    config already carries them; no Polaris biometric capability is implied.", "  - **(B) Scope facial recognition into v1 \u2014 1/10.** Pros: anticipates a plausible law-enforcement ask.", "    Cons: unrequested (no program-record requirement); the policy/compliance surface would dominate the", "    media workstream; capability unverified in-boundary; and a wrong face match is the highest-cost error", "    this pipeline could emit.", "- **M-7 \u2014 Cross-track timeline assembly for video \u2014 RESOLVED 2026-07-20 \u2192 A** (product owner; dated STATE", "  entry): no third artifact \u2014 the platform read path owns the merge via a **deterministic", "  time-ordered-union read contract** (now specified \u2014 \u00a77.6), with the guarantee that no AI consumer is", "  ever handed parallel streams to merge. The M-2 write-time principle is clarified as scoped to intra-artifact modeling (see", "  the M-2 entry above and STATE). Options kept below for the record. \u2014 Original framing: a processed video", "  yields two time-coded streams: the transcript (audio track \u2014 one artifact, M-2) and the visual track's", "  per-frame detections + promoted events (\u00a75). The recorded M-2 principle \u2014 *timelines are assembled at", "  write time, never zipped by a model in context* \u2014 was resolved for parallel **audio** outputs; the", "  cross-track question is new: what does a consumer receive when it asks \"what happened in this footage\"?", "  Every option below honors the principle's intent (a model must never be handed parallel streams to", "  merge); they differ on **where** the single ordered stream is materialized.", "  - **(A) No third artifact \u2014 the platform read path owns the zip \u2014 7/10, recommended.** Transcript", "    segments and visual detections/events are all time-locatored members in the SoR and project to the hot", "    store; a **deterministic time-ordered union** \u2014 one query primitive with fixed ordering rules (media", "    timeline position; tie-break by track, then member key) \u2014 is the single stream every consumer receives", "    (evidence display, Investigate tools, L3/L4 context). Pros: no denormalized third artifact to", "    re-version whenever either track reprocesses (a late high-quality ASR pass would otherwise fan into", "    timeline rewrites); one assembly rule serves *any* time range, including cross-item windows (\"this", "    street, 02:00\u201303:00\" spans multiple videos \u2014 a per-video artifact cannot serve that query anyway).", "    Cons: the ordered-union primitive must be built, tested, and owned as a platform read contract (the", "    Apollo PRD consumes it); \"assembled at write\" is honored in substance \u2014 order derives entirely from", "    written time codes \u2014 but there is no stored timeline row.", "  - **(B) Materialized `media_timeline` artifact per video (write-time zip) \u2014 4/10.** Pros: the timeline", "    is literally an artifact \u2014 simplest custody-presentation story, one row to render. Cons: pure", "    denormalization (every member duplicates a member that already exists elsewhere); reprocessing either", "    track forces timeline re-versioning; does nothing for cross-item time queries, so the read primitive", "    gets built anyway \u2014 the artifact buys rendering convenience at permanent double-write cost.", "  - **(C) Extend the transcript into the full media timeline (visual lines inline) \u2014 2/10.** Pros: one", "    artifact, an already-resolved shape. Cons: overloads M-2's resolution (visual detections are not", "    captions); couples visual reprocessing to transcript versions; a silent video would need a \"transcript\"", "    with no audio in it.", "- **M-8 \u2014 Long-running/live stream shape \u2014 RESOLVED 2026-07-26** (product owner; dated STATE entry):", "  stable stream registration \u2192 finite immutable chunk source items under continuity epochs (\u00a77.7);", "  source-bounded physical chunk profile + operation-posture override, independent analysis and clip", "  windows; detections visible per committed chunk, event promotion after its aggregation window, clip", "  resolution after post-roll as an ordered bundle of parent-owned parts; emergent/standard/bulk overload", "  behavior with explicit coverage; zero or one optional operation per epoch in V1 with boundary-clamped", "  windows; customer rewind or a signed bounded ephemeral buffer for pre-roll, with hold extension limited", "  to finishing already-requested clips. Cross-chunk event identity is stream-epoch/window-owned, not", "  assigned to an arbitrary chunk. At sharded scale, epoch work uses control-shard admission shadows with", "  receipts to chunk shards. Exact late gap fills auto-process only inside a source-configured horizon;", "  afterward bytes remain evidence and changing outputs requires explicit re-extraction. The 2026-07-27", "  adversarial fold made that automatic path a bounded correction generation with an abort/release outcome,", "  added epoch-time capture-gap/overlap truth, and kept control indexing at chunk/stage receipt grain; these", "  are mechanism corrections, not new product choices. M-8 resolves the design shape only; \u00a77.7's", "  need-triggered phasing governs whether it is built.", "- **Verify (external):** GovCloud GPU capacity/quotas for in-VPC CV \u2014 *availability half verified", "  2026-07-21* (G4dn/G6/Gr6 inference-class in both gov regions; no G5/G6e/Inf2 \u2014 \u00a710.2); account quota", "  values remain in-account (\u00a710.5). Bedrock account-level TPM/RPM quotas", "  (binding for any hosted arm at scale \u2014 \u00a77.4). *Nova FedRAMP \u2014 verified 2026-07-20:* **not authorized**", "  (absent from AWS's Bedrock-models certification page, last updated 2026-07-14) \u2014 now a watch item;", "  native-video in-boundary is gated on it. *Claude vision in-boundary:* Claude models through 4.6 are", "  FedRAMP High in GovCloud (same page); verify in-account that image input is enabled on GovCloud", "  endpoints. *Managed ASR \u2014 verified 2026-07-20:* Amazon Transcribe is in-region in both GovCloud regions", "  and FedRAMP-authorized (\u00a76.4); confirm the effective feature set in-account (the program's standing rule", "  for authorization lists). *Nova pricing in GovCloud regions:* commercial rates verified (\u00a77.4); gov-region", "  rates typically run higher \u2014 confirm in-account.", "", "## 5. Image pipeline (authored 2026-07-20)", "", "The dependency root: video's visual track reduces to sampled frames fed through this pipeline (\u00a73); the", "ingestion extraction-&-persistence chunk consumes these shapes (ingestion \u00a74.2\u2013\u00a74.6). Three feeders, one", "pipeline: (a) standalone image source items (evidence photos, document scans, uploaded images); (b) sampled", "frames from video active segments (orchestration is the video chunk's; per-image processing is identical);", "(c) stills materialized from `external_reference` sources. Input invariant: extraction reads only promoted", "evidence objects or a policy-authorized acquisition (ingestion \u00a73.0); frames/stills we retain ride the same", "quarantine \u2192 promote path before analysis. For external originals, Tier-0 decode uses controlled dereference:", "the source's `dereference_policy` must permit the fetch, expected hash/version is verified where supplied,", "untrusted decode is sandboxed, and the immutable acquisition intent/result records the terminal outcome and,", "for a successful fetch, its transient/durable disposition and scan/structural verdict. Everything from Tier 1", "on reads only the exact object version after it enters", "scanned-transient staging or durable evidence, or a derivative promoted through the same gate.", "", "### 5.1 The funnel applied to one image", "", "| Tier | Runs | Produces |", "|---|---|---|", "| **0 \u2014 deterministic (CPU, near-free)** | decode/integrity validation; format normalization; EXIF/XMP metadata extraction (capture time, GPS, device \u2014 extracted *claims*, stamped like any field, \u00a75.3); perceptual-hash **dedup hint** (never identity \u2014 ingestion \u00a74.1); quality gates (resolution/blur/exposure) that short-circuit model spend on unusable images (config) | go/no-go + capture-metadata fields |", "| **1 \u2014 in-VPC CV (GPU, cheap)** | detection over the context's target classes (\u00a75.2); multi-object tracking when the feeder is a frame stream (track ids group per-frame detections); plate reading (detection + OCR specialization) | structured detections: class, bbox, confidence, track, attributes |", "| **2 \u2014 premium, selective** | OCR (document/scene text) per policy; VLM description / attribute enrichment on flagged detections/frames, per policy + per-item/per-hour budget caps | OCR blocks; description fields |", "", "Tier-1/2 model selection (detector, tracker, OCR engine, VLM) is an **eval + screening item** \u2014 license,", "GovCloud deployability, GPU footprint \u2014 owned by the GovCloud-serving chunk (\u00a710). No model quality claims", "are made here; the settled serving posture stands (in-VPC CV at firehose scale, Nova-class/hosted VLM spent", "selectively \u2014 \u00a72).", "", "### 5.2 Extraction targets by context (defaults \u2014 per-source config, not architecture)", "", "The DATA-12 onboarding config names the context; the context selects the default target set. Every row", "below is a **default**, overridable per source and validated in the onboarding dry-run (FR-2.4):", "", "| Context class | Tier 0 | Tier 1 targets | Tier 2 defaults |", "|---|---|---|---|", "| `cctv_fixed` (surveillance / canvass) | quality gates; overlay detection | persons, vehicles, plates | OCR of burned-in timestamp / camera-id overlay; VLM only on promoted detections |", "| `body_cam` | quality gates | persons, vehicles, plates; weapon-class objects (*candidate class \u2014 model availability/quality is an eval item, not asserted*) | opportunistic scene OCR (signage, documents in frame); VLM on flagged frames |", "| `evidence_photo` | EXIF (capture time / GPS) | objects per config; plates / VIN / serials | full-image OCR **default-on**; VLM description **default-on** (low volume, high value per image) |", "| `document_scan` | page splitting | minimal detection | full OCR \u2192 text-path handoff (\u00a75.5) \u2014 the document's *content* is the payload |", "| `aerial_satellite` | georeferencing metadata | objects (vehicles, structures) per config | change detection needs a registered baseline series \u2014 a **reviewed extension** (ingestion \u00a71), not a v1 default |", "", "New context classes are configuration when their targets stay inside the supported class set; novel", "semantics (new model classes, new modalities-within-images) are reviewed extensions \u2014 the ingestion \u00a73.2", "cost curve applies unchanged.", "", "### 5.3 The `image_analysis` artifact (conforms to ingestion \u00a73.5)", "", "Strict publication does not wait for a model finding. Before any model-backed image analysis, Tier 0 writes a", "deterministic **`media_source_manifest` base artifact** in the same Accelerate transaction as the canonical", "source receipt. For a standalone image it records format, dimensions, declared/captured metadata as attributed", "claims, evidence pointer/disposition, and the planned capability set. For finite video/audio it records the", "container, duration, tracks, time base, and evidence pointer/disposition. The manifest is schema-valid even when", "later analysis is empty, skipped, or fails; it is not a fabricated finding. Media analysis coverage and findings", "are follow-on outputs under ingestion \u00a73.5's three completion classes.", "", "One registered artifact type (F-ING-9 registry: schema + description + query/index hints + reasoning", "hints) carrying everything the tiers produced for one image. *Shape per fork M-4, **resolved 2026-07-20", "\u2192 A** (one artifact per analyzed image; member-keyed collections \u2014 dated STATE entry).*", "", "**What counts as a detection.** One **located, confidence-scored, model-attributed assertion instance** in", "one image: (class, bbox, confidence, producing model/tier) plus class-specific attributes (e.g.", "`plate_text`). Three people in one frame = three detections; the *same* object across sampled frames =", "many detections sharing one `track_id` \u2014 the **track**, not the detection, is the unit promotion", "aggregates on (\u00a75.4). OCR blocks and VLM descriptions are sibling member kinds under the same addressing \u2014", "located, scored assertions that aren't object-class instances. A detection is an assertion (\"the detector", "claims a person is here at 0.87\"), never a fact and never an entity (entities come only through the M-5", "handle gate). Everything the tiers find therefore lives *inside* the image's artifact row as an", "addressable member \u2014 the M-4 rationale: nothing leaves the row without a contribution-row pointer back to", "its exact member path.", "", "- **Grain:** one artifact per analyzed image **with findings** (STATE 2026-07-21). Per-frame execution truth\u2014", "  analyzed-empty vs skipped vs failed, run identity pinned\u2014remains in the ledger manifest. Accelerate's", "  source-item capability row records bounded agent-facing semantic coverage. A registration exposing the \u00a77.6", "  union read declares a versioned, labeled `media_analysis_coverage` artifact as `required_follow_on`; the", "  worker publishes it in a complete follow-on transaction before marking that capability terminal-success,", "  and the hot store projects that canonical artifact. Until then \u00a77.6 returns typed `coverage_pending` from", "  the source-item coverage row. The hot store never treats raw ledger rows as agent-facing truth. \"No findings\"", "  is a model assertion at recorded thresholds, never ground truth. Batch/segment coarsening for frame streams", "  is the video chunk's dial on this same grain (M-4 option C note).", "- **Canonical Pydantic schema** (JSONB-backed values are Pydantic-typed \u2014 no DB enum mirrors), members", "  addressed by stable member key per ingestion \u00a73.5:", "  - `source` \u2014 source-item reference + locator in the canonical media-locator grammar (ingestion \u00a73.5):", "    `video;t=<ms>` for video-derived frames; `page[<n>]` for multi-page scans; null for whole standalone", "    images. The locator doubles as the artifact's **slot discriminator** (ingestion \u00a74.1): the slot key", "    `(source_item_id, image_analysis, locator)` names this analysis deterministically \u2014 reprocessing the", "    same frame re-versions the same slot, never a sibling artifact", "  - `detections.<detection_id>` \u2014 class, bbox, confidence, `track_id?`, producing tier, attributes", "    (e.g. `plate_text` + issuing region for plate reads)", "  - `ocr.<block_id>` \u2014 text, bbox, confidence, language, kind (`overlay_timestamp` | `document` | `scene` |", "    `plate` | `serial`)", "  - `descriptions.<desc_id>` \u2014 VLM outputs (the producing skill/prompt version rides `run_id`)", "  - `capture_metadata` \u2014 EXIF-derived fields", "- **Contribution rows** (ingestion \u00a73.5, one per stamped field): `source_kind=source_item`; `source_id` =", "  the image's (or, for frames, the video's) `source_item_id` + version; `source_locator` = the locator", "  above when finer than whole-item (`source_field_path` stays null \u2014 a locator is never a field path,", "  ingestion \u00a73.5); `run_id` = a UUID naming the planning-time model/weights, skill/prompt/config/capability", "  versions and run-plan digest; `executed_at` is run metadata, never identity (bitwise GPU determinism is not claimed);", "  `contributed_labels` = the source item's effective labels (whole-item inheritance; finer-grained only", "  when the source supplies finer); `policy_version` pinned.", "- **Versioning:** reprocessing under a new model/config writes a new `artifact_version` with a supersession", "  pointer (\u00a73.5); member ids are stable within a version, not across versions. **Cross-version member", "  correspondence is asserted, never assumed (2026-07-21, pass-3):** the superseding version's supersession", "  record carries a member mapping \u2014 `same` / `changed` / `removed` / `new` \u2014 computed at write time from", "  deterministic evidence only: handle equality (plate text, VIN, GPS), track time-overlap/IoU as", "  correspondence *hints* \u2014 never bare member-key equality (model-assigned ids don't survive re-runs, and", "  visual re-identification is a capability this program does not assume: the M-5 option-B rejection).", "  Unmatched members are `removed`/`new`. The mapping drives the ingestion \u00a73.5 fan-out cascade: mapped", "  members re-version their promoted events/observations, removed members retract them, and the \u00a75.5 chained", "  text artifacts follow the same rules transitively.", "- **Time is claims, not truth:** burned-in overlay timestamps and EXIF times are extracted fields with", "  confidence \u2014 they never overwrite the envelope's trusted timestamps (ingestion \u00a74). Both persist; a", "  mismatch is investigative signal, not a write conflict.", "- **Transaction:** artifact row + contribution rows + effective-label map + **SoR-local outbox events**", "  commit atomically; fail closed (ingestion \u00a73.5 \u2014 the intake-ledger outbox is a different cluster and", "  follows idempotently, never in this transaction). One image = one transaction.", "", "### 5.4 Entity observations & event promotion", "", "- **Entity minting is identity-handle-gated (M-5, resolved 2026-07-20 \u2192 A):** a detection mints an", "  **entity-observation artifact** \u2014 assertion semantics; `ingest.artifacts` is its sole generic", "  identity/version/provenance anchor and the required one-to-one `ent` extension is its sole entity-specific", "  payload; neither can version independently, and platform-reference and tenant-profile fields are never", "  overwritten (ingestion \u00a73.5) \u2014 only when it carries a resolvable identity handle: plate string \u2192 vehicle;", "  EXIF/overlay GPS \u2192 location; OCR'd VIN/serial \u2192 vehicle/item; OCR'd *names* ride the text path's", "  existing entity extraction (\u00a75.5). Anonymous person/vehicle detections stay detections + promoted", "  events \u2014 queryable, clip-linked, no entity row. Observation labels travel with the observation.", "  Resolve-or-mint scope is policy-selected: exact-handle matches may auto-link only inside the same generated", "  non-null `scope_key` identity universe. A matching handle is candidate evidence, never entity uniqueness.", "  Cross-operation and operation-to-standing matches may produce a separately authorized association in Wave", "  1, but never consolidation or profile promotion (ENT-1; cross-operation visibility is policy-gated, Apollo", "  STATE D4/Q-25). **Observation identity + contribution precision (2026-07-21,", "  pass-3):** an observation's slot is its **handle key** (ingestion \u00a74.1) \u2014 (producing analysis slot,", "  handle kind, normalized handle value) \u2014 so the same plate read twice in one image is *one* observation,", "  carrying **one contribution row per supporting member** (the plate-detection bbox *and* its OCR-read", "  member both stamp rows, ingestion \u00a73.5); its effective labels join over those members' labels, and the", "  observation row + contribution rows + label map commit fail-closed like every producer. Across", "  reprocessing generations the handle key resolves through the \u00a75.3 member mapping \u2014 a re-found plate", "  re-versions its observation; a plate the new version no longer reads retracts it (ingestion \u00a73.5", "  fan-out).", "- **Event promotion is deterministic config** (the resolved M-2 pattern applied to vision): the per-source", "  config maps detection class \u2192 promotion policy \u2014 `never` | `always` | `conf \u2265 threshold` |", "  `tier2_confirmed` (a VLM look before promoting high-false-positive classes) \u2014 with **track-scoped", "  aggregation**: one event per track per aggregation window, so a person crossing thirty sampled frames is", "  one event referencing one track, not thirty events. Standalone images promote per qualifying detection.", "  Each promotion emits its raw event under a deterministic **promotion key** (ingestion \u00a74.1) \u2014 promoting", "  slot + rule id + track or member key + window index; config versions stay in `run_id` (generation", "  identity, never logical identity) \u2014 so a retried run never double-promotes, a config change re-versions", "  or retracts existing promotion slots instead of minting parallel ones, and a reprocessed track that maps", "  `same`/`changed` re-versions its existing event rather than minting a duplicate semantic incident", "  (ingestion \u00a73.5 fan-out).", "- **Promoted events ride the standard path** \u2014 raw event \u2192 ESS \u2192 `source_events` (BRD FR-5.1) with the", "  F-ING-11 additive fields (`scope_key`, `operation_id`, security labels, source-item links, scoped-entity", "  links, and first-party artifact attachments). The", "  event's contribution rows reference the promoting members (`source_kind=artifact`,", "  `source_field_path=detections.<id>`), so the derivation is unambiguous \u2014 the same move as M-2's", "  transcript-segment references. The raw event carries the full **`upstream_contributions`** block", "  (F-ING-11 carrier contract, 2026-07-21) \u2014 every promoting member's `(artifact_type, artifact_id,", "  artifact_version, member path, labels, run_id)` \u2014 so ESS can write exact \u00a73.5 contribution rows at the", "  `source_events` write; ESS never edits the block, and merges union it.", "- **Evidence clips:** promotion emits the clip request per the M-3 policy (storage chunk); clip bytes ride", "  quarantine \u2192 promote (ingestion \u00a73.0), and the clip references its originating detections. Clips are", "  **evidence objects, not assertions** \u2014 supersession never retracts them: a clip whose originating", "  detections are `removed` in a later analysis version keeps its bytes and its historical references", "  (custody intact); it simply stops being reachable from the *current* version's members.", "", "### 5.5 OCR \u2192 text-path handoff (one extraction stack, chained artifacts)", "", "OCR output that constitutes readable text re-enters the **standard text-extraction path** as a derived", "source: text-extraction skills run over the `image_analysis` OCR fields, and their outputs stamp", "contribution rows with `source_kind=artifact` pointing at the OCR member path \u2014 the \u00a73.5 chain intact", "(entity/event \u2190 text extraction \u2190 OCR block \u2190 image \u2190 source item). The image pipeline never grows its own", "text-entity extractor; names, addresses, and identifiers inside OCR'd text are minted by the same skills", "that mint them from any text item. Chained artifacts are slots like any other (ingestion \u00a74.1): the", "discriminator is the **derivation path** \u2014 (upstream slot, upstream member path) \u2014 so re-extraction over", "the same OCR member re-versions the same chained artifact, and a `removed` OCR member retracts its chain", "transitively (ingestion \u00a73.5 fan-out) \u2014 corrected OCR never leaves stale extracted entities live.", "", "### 5.6 Per-source config surface (DATA-12)", "", "The keys the image pipeline resolves at dispatch. Config is reviewed, versioned data (ingestion \u00a73.2);", "every analysis run pins its config version in `run_id`.", "", "| Config block | Keys (representative) |", "|---|---|", "| `context` | `context_class` \u2014 selects the \u00a75.2 defaults |", "| `tier0` | quality-gate thresholds (min resolution, blur); EXIF policy; dedup-hint policy |", "| `tier1` | model profile; target class set; per-class **threshold pairs** (record floor < report threshold \u2014 near-misses persist as low-confidence members, STATE 2026-07-21); tracking on/off |", "| `tier2` | `ocr_policy` (`off` / `overlay_only` / `flagged` / `always`); `vlm_policy` (`off` / `promoted_only` / `flagged` / `always`); per-item + per-hour budget caps |", "| `promotion` | class \u2192 event-type map; per-class promotion policy + thresholds; aggregation window |", "| `entities` | enabled identity handles (M-5 \u2192 A: plate / GPS / VIN / serial; anonymous detections never mint) |", "| `sampling` | frame-sampling keys ride this same config block; semantics + defaults (rates by context) are the **video chunk's** |", "| `evidence` | analyzed-frame/still retention policy (retained frames are evidence-lake objects, ingestion \u00a73.0); clip-policy pointer (M-3 \u2192 \u00a79) |", "", "Budget caps are the per-source expression of the funnel's economics (M-1's \"best data per dollar-hour\"", "frame); the onboarding dry-run report (FR-2.4) shows the operator what each tier produced and spent before", "a config goes live.", "", "## 6. Audio pipeline (authored 2026-07-20 \u2014 M-2 fixed the shape; this chunk fills mechanics, schema, promotion)", "", "Feeders: standalone audio source items (calls, interviews, dispatch recordings) and the audio track of", "video (dual-track orchestration is the video chunk's; per-stream processing is identical).", "", "### 6.1 Pipeline shape \u2014 assembled at write", "", "| Stage | Runs | Notes |", "|---|---|---|", "| **Tier 0 \u2014 deterministic** | decode/validate; voice-activity (VAD) segmentation; channel handling | silence drops before any model spends anything \u2014 the funnel applied to audio. Multi-channel sources whose channels are distinct speakers (phone-call legs) process per channel, declared in config |", "| **Tier 1** | diarization + ASR over speech segments; **acoustic event detection (AED)** over the full stream in parallel (gunshot / glass-break / alarm-class sounds \u2014 class set per config) | model selection (ASR, diarizer, AED) is an eval + screening item (GovCloud-serving chunk), the \u00a75.1 rule |", "| **Tier 2 \u2014 selective** | re-transcription of low-confidence segments with a premium model; language ID + translation per config | budget-capped like \u00a75.6 |", "", "The merge into **one** time-coded artifact happens **at write**: speech segments and non-speech sound", "descriptions interleave on a single caption-style timeline (M-2, resolved \u2014 timelines are assembled at", "write time, never zipped in model context). A late, better pass (a slow high-quality ASR re-run) is a", "**new artifact version** with a supersession pointer \u2014 never a second timeline.", "", "### 6.2 The `transcript` artifact (conforms to ingestion \u00a73.5)", "", "Registered type `transcript` (a top-level \u00a73.5 registry entry, like `image_analysis`); one per audio source", "item \u2014 or per audio *track* of a video item. The track index is the **slot discriminator** (ingestion", "\u00a74.1): slot key `(source_item_id, transcript, audio[<i>])`, `<i>` = zero-based container demux order \u2014 one", "transcript slot per track, re-versioned on reprocessing. Contribution rows point at the owning", "`source_item_id` with `source_locator` = the segment's span in the canonical grammar \u2014", "`audio[<i>];t=[start,end)`, half-open, media-internal ms (ingestion \u00a73.5; `source_field_path` stays null", "for media-stream sources).", "", "- **Members:** `segments.<segment_id>` \u2014 `t_start_ms` / `t_end_ms` (half-open: start inclusive, end", "  exclusive, matching the locator grammar); `kind` (`speech` | `non_speech`);", "  `speaker_label` (transcript-local anonymous label \u2014 \"S1\" here has no relation to \"S1\" in any other", "  transcript); `text` (speech) or `sound_class` + confidence (non-speech); `language`; ASR confidence;", "  optional word-level timings.", "- **Contribution rows / label inheritance / versioning / fail-closed transaction:** identical to \u00a75.3's", "  pattern; `run_id` carries the ASR/diarizer/AED model identities (one contribution row per producing", "  model where a segment mixes producers).", "- **Speaker identity across items is voice biometrics** \u2014 a v1 non-goal (M-6, resolved 2026-07-20), not", "  diarization's job.", "", "### 6.3 Promotion & downstream", "", "- **AED promotion is deterministic config**, mirroring \u00a75.4: sound class \u2192 event-type map, per-class", "  thresholds, aggregation over consecutive detections (one sustained alarm = one event, not one per", "  window). Promoted events reference their transcript segments via contribution rows (M-2, resolved);", "  the F-ING-11 additive fields apply, under the same deterministic promotion key and", "  `upstream_contributions` carrier as \u00a75.4 (ingestion \u00a74.1 / F-ING-11).", "- **Speech content is the text path's job:** extraction over *what was said* (names, plates read aloud,", "  threats, addresses) runs the standard text-extraction skills over the transcript artifact \u2014 the same", "  chained-artifact handoff as \u00a75.5. **M-5 gates *direct media detections* only (scope fixed 2026-07-21,", "  pass-3 minor):** a name spoken aloud is ordinary text \u2014 the text path mints person/entity observations", "  from it under its own standard contract, exactly as it would from the same sentence in a document, with", "  contribution rows pointing at the exact transcript segments. The pinned processing policy chooses", "  platform-reference matching, tenant-entity accumulation, or observation-only behavior; an operation-", "  scoped observation cannot silently link across operations or into the client-standing corpus. The audio", "  pipeline itself never interprets content.", "", "### 6.4 Serving note (verified facts; the pick belongs to the GovCloud-serving chunk)", "", "**Verified 2026-07-20** (AWS GovCloud user guide, Transcribe page; AWS FedRAMP services-in-scope):", "**Amazon Transcribe is in-region in both GovCloud regions and FedRAMP-authorized.** Gaps against our", "needs: Call Analytics is unavailable in GovCloud; automatic language identification and automatic content", "redaction are unavailable in us-gov-east-1 only (present in us-gov-west-1, our primary region); AWS states", "GovCloud AI content is not used for service improvement. Confirm the effective feature set in-account (the", "program's standing rule for authorization lists). So a managed in-boundary ASR path exists; whether its", "diarization/custom-vocabulary quality carries investigative audio, versus in-VPC open ASR/AED stacks", "(required anyway for any non-AWS/air-gapped ENV-5 boundary), is the serving chunk's eval. Non-speech", "acoustic-event description is **not** claimed as a Transcribe feature \u2014 treat AED as needing its own model", "on either path until shown otherwise.", "", "## 7. Video pipeline (authored 2026-07-20)", "", "Video is orchestration over the two pipelines already specified, plus the one genuinely new mechanic", "(deterministic segmentation + sampling) and the M-1 eval that prices the mix. Nothing here re-decides the", "committed baseline: **frame sampling into the \u00a75 image pipeline is the only committed visual path** (M-1);", "native-video is an evaluated, per-source, boundary-gated option.", "", "### 7.1 Dual-track orchestration", "", "One finite video source item fans out to two parallel tracks, each riding an already-specified pipeline.", "For an unbounded live feed, each sealed chunk is one such source item and \u00a77.7 supplies the stream-level", "identity, continuity, and cross-chunk mechanics:", "", "- **Demux (Tier 0):** container metadata (duration, resolution, codec, container timestamps \u2014 extracted", "  *claims* per \u00a75.3's rule); audio track split out \u2192 the \u00a76 audio pipeline; visual track \u2192 segmentation +", "  sampling (\u00a77.2) \u2192 the \u00a75 image pipeline per sampled frame.", "- **Time base:** the **media-internal timeline** (`t=<ms>` from stream start) is authoritative for all", "  intra-item alignment \u2014 every frame artifact locator, transcript segment, detection, and promoted event", "  uses it. Mapping media time to wall-clock is itself an extracted claim (container creation time, burned-in", "  overlay, CCTV system metadata \u2014 each with confidence), never silently trusted; the envelope's", "  `received_at` stays the only trusted platform timestamp (ingestion \u00a74).", "- **Track independence, fail-closed writes:** each track's artifacts commit in their own \u00a73.5 transactions;", "  one track failing (corrupt audio, unsupported codec) never discards the other's committed work. The video", "  processing run completes when all *planned* track writes commit \u2014 and the plan is durable: every planned", "  output (audio track, sampled frame, clip) is an entry in the delivery unit's **sub-unit manifest**", "  (ingestion \u00a74.1), each track closing its own manifest subset independently, densification closing with", "  its generation's budget window; completion is the manifest predicate (every entry terminal, no generative", "  stage still able to append) \u2014 never a worker's in-memory belief. A failed track retries idempotently", "  (ingestion \u00a74.1), and late/re-run outputs are new artifact versions with supersession \u2014 the M-2 rule,", "  applied to both tracks.", "- **Artifacts produced per video:** one deterministic `media_source_manifest` in the base-publication bundle;", "  then one `image_analysis` per analyzed frame **with findings** (B+, STATE 2026-07-21 \u2014 every analyzed frame,", "  empty included, gets a ledger-manifest coverage row; locators `video;t=<ms>`, \u00a75.3) + one `transcript` per", "  audio track (\u00a76.2, slot `audio[<i>]`) + promoted events (track-scoped", "  aggregation, \u00a75.4/\u00a76.3) + evidence clips per M-3. **No cross-track timeline artifact is materialized (M-7, resolved 2026-07-20", "  \u2192 A):** the deterministic time-ordered union over both tracks is a platform read contract \u2014 the only", "  stream any AI consumer receives (\u00a74).", "- **Coverage accounting (two grains \u2014 amended 2026-09-11):** segments Tier 0 deliberately skipped (no", "  motion, below quality gates) persist as **aggregate accounting** \u2014 time ranges, rule versions, counts", "  (the \u00a73.0 reject-accounting pattern). Every **analyzed** frame additionally gets a per-frame coverage", "  row in the **sub-unit manifest** (ingestion \u00a74.1\u2014the coverage row *is* that frame's operational outcome", "  entry): outcome (findings / empty / failed) + run identity (model, weights, config, thresholds). At source-item", "  grain, Accelerate's labeled capability-coverage row distinguishes pending/empty/output/failed/skipped. A", "  \u00a77.6-capable registry declaration publishes the registered, bounded, versioned `media_analysis_coverage`", "  artifact as a `required_follow_on` before marking the capability complete; only that canonical artifact is", "  projected to the hot store. Every negative remains an auditable model assertion at recorded thresholds, not", "  an absence of evidence.", "", "### 7.2 Segmentation & sampling mechanics (deterministic, CPU \u2014 Tier 0)", "", "- **Scene/motion segmentation:** frame-differencing + scene-cut detection over the decoded stream produces", "  **active segments** (t-ranges with an activity class: motion / scene-change / static). Sensitivity is", "  per-context config. Deterministic given (decoder, algorithm, config) \u2014 recorded in `run_id` like every", "  producer.", "- **Sampling within active segments:** base rate by context (\u00a77.3) + **densification** \u2014 a Tier-1 detection", "  in frame *f* raises the sampling rate in a window around *f* (bounded by the frame budget) so the", "  pipeline looks harder exactly where something was found. Static segments sample at a sparse keepalive", "  rate or not at all (config).", "- **Budgets bound everything:** per-item and per-hour frame budgets + token budgets (\u00a75.6 `tier2` caps)", "  make the funnel's economics enforceable per source \u2014 a runaway sampler cannot spend past its config.", "- **Materialized frames are evidence \u2014 with deterministic child identity (2026-07-21, pass-3):** every", "  sampled frame / still / audio extract / clip we retain rides quarantine \u2192 promote (ingestion \u00a73.0). Its", "  object key is **`(parent source_item_id, child kind, canonical locator, derivation digest)`** \u2014 the", "  digest hashing the deterministic derivation identity (decoder + version, extraction config version). A", "  derivation re-run lands on its own key via **conditional create** \u2014 if the object exists, verify its", "  hash: identical \u2192 adopt the existing object (no re-put); mismatch \u2192 terminal-fail + alarm", "  (same-derivation bytes must be identical; a mismatch is non-determinism or tampering \u2014 ingestion \u00a74.1).", "  The child's manifest entry records the full five-part object reference (bucket, key, object version-id,", "  content hash, size bytes). A new processing generation with a different decoder/config mints **new keys** \u2014 immutable", "  evidence is never overwritten, and bytes from a different derivation are never silently reused. Durable state lives", "  in the parent unit's sub-unit manifest (ingestion \u00a74.1): `materialized(quarantine)` \u2192", "  `promoted(evidence)` \u2192 analysis outcome. **Reconciliation:** a promoted child object with no terminal", "  manifest entry is an orphan, swept against the quarantine TTL (the \u00a74.1 rule); a manifest entry with no", "  object retries or goes terminal-failed. Retention per the `evidence` config block (\u00a75.6).", "- **Grain note (M-4 boundary):** per M-4's resolution as refined 2026-07-21 (B+), each analyzed frame", "  **with findings** gets its own `image_analysis` artifact; every analyzed frame \u2014 empty results included \u2014", "  gets a coverage row in the sub-unit manifest (\u00a77.1), so no analyzed frame is unaccounted for. Segment-grain coarsening (one artifact per segment, two-level members) is a **registered", "  contingency only** \u2014 it relaxes the owner's \"everything ties back to the image's artifact row\" rationale,", "  so pulling that lever requires a product-owner decision with measured SoR row pressure in hand; it is not", "  a v1 mechanism.", "", "### 7.3 Sampling defaults by context (config defaults, dry-run validated \u2014 not architecture)", "", "| Context class | Segmentation posture | Base sampling (active segments) | Densification |", "|---|---|---|---|", "| `cctv_fixed` | motion-gated; static majority expected | sparse (order 1 frame / 2\u20135 s) | on detection, window around hit |", "| `body_cam` | mostly-active expected; scene-cut driven | steady (order 1 frame / s) | on detection + audio-event cross-trigger (an AED gunshot densifies the visual track at that t \u2014 cross-track trigger, config) |", "| `dash_cam` | motion + scene-cut | steady | on detection |", "| `evidence_video` (uploaded clips) | minimal gating \u2014 assume relevant | dense (short, high-value) | n/a (already dense) |", "| `aerial_satellite` | per-mission config | per-mission config | per-mission config |", "", "Numbers are order-of-magnitude defaults to seed onboarding configs; the M-1 eval (\u00a77.4) is what tunes them", "per context against measured yield-per-dollar, and the dry-run report shows the operator the spend/yield", "before a config goes live (FR-2.4).", "", "### 7.4 The M-1 eval \u2014 \"best tier-mix per dollar-hour of footage\" (design; execution open)", "", "**Question (product-owner framing, 2026-07-19):** for a fixed budget per hour of footage, which tier mix", "yields the most useful extractions?", "", "**Verified inputs (2026-07-20, AWS Nova user guide + AWS/Nova pricing pages; evidence level: vendor docs,", "re-verify at eval run):**", "", "- **Nova video mechanics (Nova v1 docs):** one video per payload; \u226425 MB base64 or \u22641 GB per file via S3", "  URI; frames resized (with distortion) to 672\u00d7672; **Lite/Pro sample at 1 FPS up to 16 min, then", "  down-sample to a fixed 960 frames total** (a 1-hour video is sampled at ~0.14 FPS \u2014 one frame per ~7 s);", "  Premier holds 1 FPS to 3,200 frames; ~276,480 tokens at the 960-frame cap (~288 tokens/frame).", "  A **Nova 2** generation exists with its own video-understanding guide \u2014 the eval must run against the", "  current generation's caps, not these.", "- **Commercial on-demand pricing (per 1M tokens in/out):** Nova Pro $0.80/$3.20; Nova Lite $0.06/$0.24;", "  Nova Micro $0.035/$0.14. GovCloud rates typically run higher \u2014 in-account verify item.", "- **Derived (arithmetic only):** one 960-frame call \u2248 $0.22 input on Pro, \u2248 $0.017 on Lite; chunking one", "  hour into \u226416-min segments \u2248 4 calls \u2248 **$0.9 (Pro) / $0.07 (Lite) input per fully-processed hour**.", "  Two consequences for the eval: (1) **cost is not the native-video blocker at moderate scale \u2014 quotas and", "  boundary are** (a fully-processed hour \u2248 1.1M input tokens; account TPM/RPM quotas bind long before", "  price; firehose tiers remain in-VPC territory per the settled posture); (2) Nova runs **its own blind", "  1-FPS/960-frame sampler** after a 672\u00d7672 distortion resize \u2014 feeding it long segments delegates our", "  Tier-0 job to a sampler that can't see our context config; the eval must test whether *our* segmentation", "  + short-segment calls beat Nova's internal sampling on long segments.", "- **Boundary gate (verified 2026-07-20):** Nova is **absent** from AWS's Bedrock-models FedRAMP", "  certification page (page updated 2026-07-14) \u2192 the native-video arm is **commercial-only** until", "  authorization lands. Claude models through 4.6 are FedRAMP High in GovCloud on the same page \u2192 the", "  in-boundary hosted-VLM arm can use authorized Claude vision **on frames** (in-account verify: image", "  input enabled on GovCloud endpoints).", "", "**Arms (candidate mixes, all tuned to the same budget point):**", "", "1. **CV-only baseline:** Tier 0 segmentation + context sampling + in-VPC CV; no premium calls.", "2. **CV + selective VLM:** arm 1 + VLM description/OCR on flagged frames (the \u00a75 default posture).", "3. **Dense-frames-to-VLM:** dense sampling straight to a VLM, no CV triage \u2014 the naive arm; expected to", "   lose on cost, included to *prove* the funnel's value, not to win.", "4. **CV + native-video on active segments:** arm 1 + native-video calls on Tier-0 active segments only", "   (short segments, our sampling upstream).", "5. **Hybrid:** arm 1 + native-video on the top-K highest-activity segments + VLM on flagged frames", "   elsewhere.", "", "**Scoring (per arm \u00d7 per context class \u00d7 2\u20133 budget points, e.g. $0.10 / $1 / $5 per hour):** extraction", "quality (detection/OCR F1 against ground truth); event correctness (promoted events vs ground-truth", "incidents); **temporal reasoning** (a fixed question set only answerable from sequence \u2014 \"did the person", "exit before the vehicle arrived\"); evidence quality (\u00a73.5 stamping completeness; clip usefulness);", "determinism/reproducibility (re-run variance at fixed model identity); cost/hour (all-in: compute + tokens)", "and wall-clock. Native-video arms are additionally scored on **provenance resolution** \u2014 a native-video", "answer attributes to a *segment*, not a frame+bbox; \u00a73.5 contribution rows for its outputs can only carry", "segment-range locators (`source_locator` = `video;t=[a,b)` \u2014 the canonical grammar's half-open range,", "coarser than a frame instant), which is a real evidence-quality cost the score must capture, not a", "footnote.", "", "**Inputs required before execution (external asks):** a ground-truth-labeled footage corpus per context", "class (representative CCTV / body-cam / evidence clips \u2014 sourced from Apollo/TBI samples or licensed", "public datasets; licensing screened); DATA-1-class volume expectations to weight the quota analysis;", "in-account quota + GovCloud pricing numbers.", "", "**Deliverable:** per-context recommended default mix, shipped as the \u00a75.6/\u00a77.3 onboarding config defaults;", "native-video enters a source's config only where the eval shows it wins within budget **and** the boundary", "allows it. The eval is the resolution mechanism for M-1's remaining open half \u2014 no mix is committed here.", "", "### 7.5 Video-specific config keys (extends the \u00a75.6 surface)", "", "| Config block | Keys (representative) |", "|---|---|", "| `segmentation` | algorithm profile; sensitivity per activity class; min-segment length |", "| `sampling` | base rate per context; densification window + multiplier; static-segment keepalive; per-item + per-hour frame budgets |", "| `tracks` | visual / audio / both; cross-track triggers (AED \u2192 visual densification, \u00a77.3) |", "| `native_video` | `off` / `eval` / `per_segment_class` (boundary-gated; commercial-only until Nova authorization); max segment length per call |", "| `live_transport` | registered compatibility-entry id/version: protocol + transport mode, authentication/credential binding, container/codecs, reconnect/continuity semantics, source backpressure behavior, and copy vs reference/rewind posture; no protocol is implied by \u00a77.7 |", "| `live_stream` | physical chunk profile (target/min/max duration + byte cap, keyframe/GOP bound, inactivity close); continuity/reconnect rules; allowed lateness + bounded late-processing horizon; checkpoint/warm-up retention and parent processing-availability/archive guarantee; customer rewind capability or ephemeral-buffer policy |", "| `live_overload` | standard-lag bound; ordered degradation rungs + minimum coverage floor; catch-up/re-extraction eligibility |", "| `timeline` | none \u2014 M-7 \u2192 A stores no timeline; the time-ordered-union read contract is platform-fixed, not per-source config (\u00a77.6) |", "", "### 7.6 The time-ordered-union read contract (M-7 \u2192 A made implementable \u2014 2026-07-21, closing the pass-3 M-7 finding)", "", "The platform read primitive every consumer receives \u2014 the Apollo PRD's consumers (evidence display,", "Investigate tools, L3/L4 context) consume it; media/ingestion owns its definition (M-7 resolution, STATE", "2026-07-20). It is served from the hot projection (ingestion \u00a73.1), but the ordering rule is a pure", "function of stored data, so SoR and projection always agree. Deterministic end to end: same stored data +", "same parameters \u2192 the same ordered stream, every time.", "", "**Union item \u2014 one normalized shape for every member kind:**", "", "| Field | Content |", "|---|---|", "| `owner` | discriminated address: `owner_kind=source_item` + `source_item_id` for item-owned members, or `owner_kind=stream_epoch` + `stream_epoch_id` only for \u00a77.7's cross-chunk promoted event; exactly one owner id, with envelope/epoch metadata for display |", "| `track` | fixed track name: `video`, `audio[<i>]`, `promoted` |", "| `kind` | `detection` \\| `ocr` \\| `description` \\| `transcript_segment` \\| `promoted_event` |", "| `span` | `[t_start, t_end)` in media-internal ms; instants carry `t_end = t_start` |", "| `artifact` | `(artifact_type, artifact_id, artifact_version)` + the member's `field_path` |", "| `payload` | the member, verbatim from its artifact version |", "| `labels` | the member field's effective labels (read enforcement filters downstream \u2014 \u00a73.4 split) |", "| `run` | producing run identity (model, config version) |", "| `refs` | for `promoted_event`: the promoting member addresses (from `upstream_contributions`); else empty |", "", "**Version selection \u2014 current-per-slot, with an explicit as-of mode.** The default mode selects,", "independently per artifact slot, the latest non-retracted version; superseded versions are **excluded**. An", "`as_of` mode (a version-pin set / generation timestamp) reproduces any historical read deterministically \u2014", "custody presentation uses it. Because supersession is slot-grain (ingestion \u00a73.5), a current read may", "legitimately mix runs across slots (audio reprocessed, video not); every union item carries its `run`", "identity, so generation mixing is auditable rather than hidden, and a full-coverage reprocessing plan is", "the operator's lever when generation purity matters.", "", "**Ordering \u2014 total, fixed, and unique.** Ascending by `(t_start, t_end, track rank, canonical owner address,", "artifact_type, output discriminator, field_path)` \u2014 the key ends in the complete member address, so no two", "union items ever tie (2026-07-21, third-review P0: a cursor must resume at exactly one position; this", "completes M-7's \"track, then member key\" tie-break rather than changing it \u2014 the member's address *is* its", "key, now fully qualified). Intervals sort by start then end (shorter first); instants are zero-length", "intervals; track rank is the fixed enumeration `video` = 0, `audio[<i>]` = 1 + i, `promoted` = last; the", "address components compare bytewise on their canonical serializations. No parameter changes the ordering", "rule \u2014 parameters only change which items are included.", "", "**Pagination is stable.** The total order plus a **bounded snapshot token** make cursor paging", "deterministic (2026-07-21, third-review P0 \u2014 replaces the earlier first-page version-pin set, which would", "grow with result cardinality and could not protect slots first touched on later pages): the cursor carries", "the last emitted sort key plus the projection revision captured at first page (an implicit `as_of`, O(1)", "regardless of result size). For a live stream, \u00a77.7.6 expands that scalar into a fixed-width revision vector", "covering artifacts, coverage, epoch state, and clip catalog\u2014still O(1), never one pin per chunk. Every", "subsequent page evaluates version selection and coverage *as of the token* \u2014 answerable for any slot because", "versions are immutable rows (select the latest version committed at or before the token). A consumer paging", "through a window therefore reads one consistent snapshot \u2014 a", "reprocessing run landing mid-scroll never reorders, duplicates, or drops items; the next fresh query picks", "up the new current versions.", "", "**Promotion duplicates \u2014 both appear, self-identified, never silently deduped.** When the requested kind", "set includes both `promoted_event` and its underlying kinds, both appear; the event's `refs` names its", "promoting members, so collapsing is a deterministic consumer choice, not hidden primitive behavior. The", "kind set is a request parameter \u2014 per-surface defaults (e.g. L3/L4 context = `promoted_event` +", "`transcript_segment`) belong to the Apollo PRD's consumer contracts; the primitive itself never filters", "silently.", "", "**Missing and failed tracks \u2014 represented, never fabricated.** Once the registration's required coverage", "follow-on completes, the result carries a per-track **coverage header** built from the versioned, labeled", "canonical `media_analysis_coverage` artifact: per track \u2014 `absent`", "(the item has no such track),", "`failed`, or covered ranges + analyzed-empty ranges + skipped ranges (with rule versions). Silence in the", "stream is therefore distinguishable \u2014 no-audio-track vs ASR-failed vs analyzed-and-empty \u2014 each an explicit", "header fact at recorded run identity (the B+ posture, STATE 2026-07-21). DataLake2's \u00a74.1 manifest rows are", "operational inputs used to produce that artifact; they are never queried by the serving projection. Header", "facts inherit the parent item's effective labels and pass the same read enforcement as member payloads.", "Before that artifact commits, the same read returns typed `coverage_pending` from the source-item semantic", "coverage row and no range/track completeness claim.", "", "**Cross-item windows \u2014 wall-clock is an eligibility-gated extracted claim.** Within one item, ordering uses", "the media-internal timeline (\u00a77.1) \u2014 never wall-clock. A cross-item window (\"this street, 02:00\u201303:00\")", "requires each item to anchor to wall-clock, and that mapping is an extracted claim (\u00a77.1). Rule: an item is", "**eligible** for cross-item ordering only if it carries a wall-clock anchor claim at or above the", "consumer's confidence floor (a request parameter with a platform default); the primitive selects the", "highest-confidence qualifying claim, pins `(claim source, confidence, offset)` per item in the result,", "orders items by anchored wall-clock while preserving each item's internal media-time order, and returns", "non-qualifying items in a separate **unplaceable** set \u2014 never silently interleaved at a guessed position.", "Anchor claims that disagree beyond tolerance make the item unplaceable with both claims reported \u2014", "investigative signal, not a write conflict (\u00a75.3's rule).", "", "### 7.7 Long-running and live streams (authored 2026-07-26)", "", "An endless feed is not one enormous video item. That shape would leave the intake row, output manifest,", "transcript, clip plan, and processing run permanently open; it would also make retry, replay, scaling, and", "retention operate at an unbounded grain. The settled shape is **a stable stream registration producing", "finite, immutable chunk source items under a stream epoch**. Every chunk rides \u00a77.1\u2013\u00a77.6 unchanged; this", "section defines the continuity around them.", "", "**Phasing/build trigger.** This section is a conditional design contract, **not an automatic V1", "implementation commitment**. Build begins only when a validated customer/source requirement needs findings", "before a stream ends and the capability receives its own estimate, approval, DATA-1 volume/SLO inputs,", "reviewed compatibility entry, boundary evidence, and release binding. Finite/prerecorded video continues to", "use the ordinary finite-item path and does not wait for \u00a77.7. \u201cRTSP,\u201d \u201cSRT,\u201d \u201cHLS,\u201d or any other transport", "is neither promised nor selected here; the first real source contract determines which adapter/profile is", "reviewed.", "", "**Ingress flow when activated.**", "", "1. Source registration binds an authenticated customer feed to `source_system_id`, stable `stream_id`,", "   optional `operation_id`, and an exact versioned `live_transport` + physical chunk profile.", "2. The matching method adapter connects using that profile and acquires the stream epoch generation before", "   accepting sequence ownership. It receives encoded packets; Kafka/MSK and Postgres never carry video", "   payload bytes.", "3. The segmenter seals finite chunks at the configured duration/byte/keyframe boundaries. A copy source", "   conditionally writes each chunk to S3 quarantine and emits the ordinary pointer-only control envelope to", "   Kafka/MSK. An external-reference source emits the registered customer archive/rewind coordinate and", "   processes bytes only through a permitted, recorded acquisition with decode isolation; signed rolling/replay", "   scratch is used only where its profile authorizes it.", "4. The ordinary ingestion gates validate/scan/decode the chunk and promote accepted copy bytes to evidence.", "   Post-scan normalization mints the finite chunk `source_item_id`, pins config/run identity, creates its", "   manifest and epoch contribution, and registers ready work for fair admission.", "5. Admitted media workers emit chunk-local detections/transcript members immediately and update \u00a77.7's", "   bounded epoch work for cross-chunk state, window promotion, and later clip resolution.", "", "#### 7.7.1 Identity, epochs, and finite completion", "", "- **Three identities, three jobs.** `stream_id` is the stable platform registration for one logical feed", "  under `(tenant_id, source_system_id)`; `stream_epoch_id` names one continuity interval; `chunk_sequence`", "  is a zero-based, strictly increasing integer within that epoch. The source's identity mapping serializes", "  `(stream_id, stream_epoch_id, chunk_sequence)` as the chunk's stable `source_record_id`; an immutable", "  chunk uses adapter-derived `source_record_version=1`. Each chunk is therefore a create-only,", "  single-version lineage under ingestion \u00a74.10: its type-tagged version order is the fixed integer `1`;", "  ordering *between* chunks comes only from the epoch/sequence fields. Redelivery with the same bytes", "  returns the original receipt; the same identity with a different hash is a source-order conflict that", "  terminal-fails and alarms. Correcting analysis is re-extraction over the same chunk, never source version", "  2.", "- **The epoch control row is the ordering/fencing authority.** One durable row per `stream_id` carries a", "  monotonic `epoch_sequence`, active `stream_epoch_id`, lease/fence generation, next `chunk_sequence`,", "  fixed operation binding, compatible physical-profile set, and open/closing/closed state. A segmenter must", "  hold the generation to reserve/seal a sequence or close the epoch; each chunk stamps it. Compare-and-swap", "  advances sequence/state, stale writers are rejected, and a same-sequence retry must present the same", "  hash. The DATA-4 build contract fixes lease acquisition, renewal cadence, maximum hold, and", "  loss-of-connection behavior; a segmenter that loses generation stops sealing, re-resolves placement, and", "  reacquires rather than draining buffered bytes under stale authority. A closed epoch rejects new sequence", "  allocation but may accept an exact late fill for a previously", "  terminalized gap through a reconciliation CAS against the current closed generation **inside the", "  source-configured late-processing horizon**; it never reopens or changes the epoch binding. The sealed", "  base epoch-work manifest stays immutable: the fill uses a deterministic bounded late-generation manifest", "  keyed by `(stream_epoch_id, gap chunk_sequence, late generation)`, while required checkpoint/warm-up", "  state is retained through the horizon. After the horizon, a first-arriving chunk is retained and exposed", "  as late evidence/coverage only; changing derived outputs requires explicit re-extraction, which builds a", "  new epoch-reprocessing manifest under ordinary bulk admission. `stream_epoch_id` is identity;", "  `epoch_sequence` is chronology.", "  This is a bounded **automatic correction generation**, not incomplete-work replay and not", "  operator-requested re-extraction. Its id is", "  `hash(base epoch-manifest digest, gap chunk_sequence, admitted chunk hash, pinned run-plan digest)`;", "  redelivery returns that generation. It deterministically plans the fill and affected successor", "  stateful entries through a captured analysis frontier, and each new attempt `run_id` derives from", "  `(late-generation id, stage id, chunk/window address, pinned plan digest)`. Existing generation attempts", "  remain immutable/no-op on retry.", "", "  Correction admission first reserves its declared cost and proves the source's correction deadline can", "  still be met; only then does it take the affected stage's epoch-generation fence at a sequence boundary.", "  Stateless per-chunk work may continue, but later stateful entries wait. The worker restores the latest", "  committed checkpoint strictly before the gap and runs the new attempts output-first, re-versioning or", "  retracting every changed stream-window slot. A stage may stop before the captured frontier only when its", "  activation contract declares reproducible canonical-state comparison and both the authenticated", "  **plaintext state digest** and complete output-address/content-digest set equal the prior generation;", "  ciphertext digest is never used. Other stages run through the captured frontier.", "", "  The correction carries a fixed attempt budget and deadline bounded by the signed horizon. Success", "  generation-CAS-installs the corrected current checkpoint and releases queued progression. Exhaustion,", "  unavailable replay substrate, or deadline breach atomically releases the fence, records", "  `partial(late_fill_unapplied)` over the affected range, leaves the late chunk as evidence-only, and", "  resumes queued live work; it never strands an epoch. Old checkpoint/output markers remain addressable", "  through the horizon, and fence age/deadline breach alarms independently of coverage-floor alarms.", "- **One finite source item per sealed chunk.** Each chunk receives its own `delivery_unit_id` and", "  `source_item_id`, promoted/reference evidence address, sub-unit manifest, run plan, and terminal", "  completion. The stream registration is configuration/control state, not a permanently-open source item,", "  and an open epoch is not a reason to hold a chunk transaction open.", "- **Epoch boundaries are provenance boundaries.** First activation starts an epoch. An explicit source", "  discontinuity, an unprovable reconnect/time-base reset, an operation-binding change, or an incompatible", "  codec/physical-chunk-profile change closes the current epoch and starts another. A transport reconnect", "  that proves packet/timestamp continuity may remain in the epoch. Closing records the last sealed", "  sequence and reason (`ended`, `discontinuity`, `inactivity`, `binding_change`, `config_change`,", "  `source_failure`); inactivity closure is configuration, and a later return starts a new epoch. Close", "  follows ingestion \u00a74's fenced `open \u2192 closing \u2192 SoR clamp mirror acknowledged \u2192 closed` handshake; a", "  replacement epoch does not activate before that acknowledgement.", "- **Operation is optional and fixed within an epoch.** The authenticated stream registration supplies zero", "  or one `operation_id` in V1. Every chunk inherits that value; a stream not strictly associated with an", "  operation stores null; operation-scoped hold/destruction then does not select it, while", "  source-system/stream/epoch and tenant scopes still do. Rebinding starts a new epoch rather than", "  retroactively changing old chunks.", "  Concurrent multi-operation association remains ingestion F-ING-12-deferred. At the binding boundary,", "  old-epoch aggregation and clip windows clamp and close with explicit partial/unavailable coverage; no", "  old-operation output may read packets from the new epoch.", "", "#### 7.7.2 Physical chunk sealing is separate from analysis windows", "", "The physical chunk profile exists to bound source-item completion and source-to-finding latency. It declares", "a target/min/max duration, maximum bytes, keyframe/GOP wait bound, and inactivity timeout. The segmenter", "requests the target boundary and seals at a valid packet/keyframe boundary; the manifest records requested", "and actual epoch-time ranges, codec/container facts, byte/hash evidence, and source-reported discontinuity.", "Sealing sequence N also compares its normalized epoch start with sequence N\u22121's end under the profile's", "tolerance. A positive delta records a typed `capture_gap`; a negative delta records `capture_overlap` and", "the deterministic canonical chunk/range election used by stateful stages. Either is coverage truth even", "when chunk sequences are contiguous; neither may be represented as \u201canalyzed with no finding.\u201d A missing", "keyframe beyond the declared bound is a source/codec conformance failure, never an unbounded open chunk.", "Each copied chunk still passes ingestion \u00a73.0's configured validation/malware gate before evidence promotion", "or analysis publication. External-reference live bytes use a registered dereference policy and append-only", "acquisition; they become accepted evidence only when the acquisition outcome is durable and the ordinary", "promotion gate succeeds. A transient acquisition may support permitted processing but is never represented as", "durably retained source evidence. Live activation capacity-prices this gate rather than bypassing it for latency.", "", "Configuration resolves in this order: platform context-class defaults \u2192 tenant/source physical profile \u2192", "the authorized operation posture or temporary source-window assertion from ingestion \u00a74.18.7. The posture", "may select only a registered override inside the source profile's signed min/max/byte bounds; an arbitrary", "per-operation-id duration is not a config surface. The resolved profile id/version/binding is pinned on the", "chunk plan and `run_id`.", "", "Physical chunks do **not** define semantic windows. Scene/motion segments, tracking windows, transcript", "segments, event-aggregation windows, native-video call windows, and evidence pre/post-roll windows retain", "their own versioned policies and may cross chunk boundaries. The resolved analysis/aggregation policy is", "pinned for the epoch. Activating an incompatible window policy closes/clamps the old epoch under reason", "`config_change` and starts the new policy on a fresh epoch; historical changes remain explicit", "re-extraction. No mid-epoch policy edit renumbers existing stream-window slots or orphans a checkpoint", "chain.", "", "#### 7.7.3 Time, continuity, and cross-chunk state", "", "Each chunk keeps the canonical chunk-local locator grammar (`video;t=<ms>`, `audio[i];t=[a,b)`) so every", "artifact still addresses one finite parent item. The platform constructs one strictly monotonic epoch", "timeline by normalizing and unwrapping the declared transport timestamps (including MPEG-TS/RTP counter", "wrap); an unexplained reset/non-monotonic jump is a sealing conformance failure and closes the epoch as a", "discontinuity. The chunk manifest carries `epoch_start_ms`/`epoch_end_ms` plus a **per-track epoch offset**", "derived from each track's first access unit. The physical profile declares whether a partial audio access", "unit is carried or truncated and the maximum accumulated A/V drift; stateful inputs use the canonical", "range election recorded for any `capture_overlap`.", "", "The source's wall-clock mapping remains an extracted claim with source/confidence per \u00a77.1; it is never", "promoted to trusted time merely because the feed is live. Where no source anchor exists, Polaris may also", "record a platform-derived bounded anchor from authenticated receipt time, maximum chunk duration, measured", "transport delay, and clock-skew envelope. Queries use it only when their declared confidence/error threshold", "accepts that bound.", "", "Stateful processors\u2014tracking, diarization, ASR continuation, aggregation, densification, and clip", "coalescing\u2014store immutable checkpoint objects under", "`(tenant_id, stream_epoch_id, epoch_generation, stage_id, run/config version,", "through_chunk_sequence, attempt_id)`. The tenant/stream/epoch prefix keeps even pre-commit orphans", "enumerable for lifecycle actions. A separate fenced **current-checkpoint pointer row** owns progression by", "`(stream_epoch_id, stage_id, run/config version)`; each stage-attempt row contains the predecessor", "checkpoint's authenticated canonical plaintext-state digest/pointer, expected output families, attempt id,", "and state `claimed \u2192 outputs_committed \u2192 checkpoint_advanced`.", "", "The no-2PC progression is output-first and loss-proof:", "", "1. The worker materializes the next normally encrypted checkpoint object under the attempt's deterministic", "   address and records an authenticated canonical plaintext-state digest; encryption need not and must not", "   be weakened merely to make ciphertext hashes repeat.", "2. One SoR transaction writes all artifact/contribution/label outputs under their deterministic attempt", "   keys, an attempt commit marker containing the exact committed output keys + checkpoint digest/pointer,", "   and the SoR-local outbox fact.", "3. The idempotent relay registers that marker in the ledger. Only after every marker/publication implied by", "   the attempt is registered may a generation-checked CAS advance the stage checkpoint/sequence.", "", "A crash before step 2 leaves no committed output; a crash after step 2 but before step 3 is repaired by the", "outbox; a retry adopts the existing commit marker and outputs, then advances the checkpoint. A checkpoint", "digest alone is never completion. A checkpoint object with no committed marker is operational orphan", "scratch and expires through reconciliation; tenant/stream/epoch-prefix enumeration also purges it during", "destruction even when no manifest row exists. A marker whose object is absent blocks advancement and alarms.", "Checkpoint objects are tenant/operation-scoped, destruction-fenced, and prunable only after the maximum of", "their ordinary replay/warm-up window and the source's late-processing horizon\u2014they are not evidence. Stages", "declare whether they require the predecessor checkpoint or can", "fan out statelessly. Recovery may replay a bounded predecessor warm-up range, but deterministic ownership", "assigns each output once to the chunk/window that contains its closing boundary; overlap is context, never", "duplicate output. No state or track identity crosses an epoch boundary unless a later, explicit correlation", "capability links the resulting observations.", "", "Cross-chunk work never keeps or reopens a chunk's intake manifest. A durable **epoch-work manifest** owns", "stateful windows, checkpoints, pending clip requests, bundle plans, and their attempt/publication fences.", "Every entry carries `tenant_id`, the epoch's nullable `operation_id`, `policy_version`, current destruction", "epochs, and effective labels. Source/control-only entries inherit the epoch anchor labels; entries with", "chunk contributions materialize the deterministic restrictive join and recompute it from surviving", "contributions when destruction removes one\u2014stale over-restriction is not treated as correct state.", "The finite chunk manifest becomes terminal after its own outputs and its idempotent contribution handoff to", "the named epoch-work entries commit. A clip part cut from that chunk later is tracked by the epoch bundle", "entry and retained child-evidence catalog while referencing the immutable parent; it is not appended to the", "already-sealed chunk manifest. Epoch close requires every window/request entry terminal or explicitly", "partial/unavailable, but old chunk completion never waits for the endless feed.", "", "The handoff also creates a bounded **processing-availability lease** for parent bytes/reference access", "already required by that epoch-work entry. Its deadline is fixed from the signed maximum aggregation +", "post-roll + permitted lag + finalization bound, or gap timeout + late-processing horizon + maximum automatic", "replay/finalization margin, whichever is later; activation fails unless local retention or the registered", "customer archive guarantees at least that availability. The same bound retains predecessor checkpoint", "history required for correction. Ordinary expiry waits for an active lease, but an", "authorized destruction order still wins (subject to the existing legal-hold rules) and resolves dependent", "work partial/unavailable. A lease cannot authorize new analysis/clip requests or extend beyond its", "precomputed deadline.", "", "#### 7.7.4 Findings, promotion, and clips while the feed is still running", "", "- **Detections do not wait for the stream or epoch to end.** A sealed chunk's frame-analysis and transcript", "  members commit as soon as that chunk's planned analysis commits. The live query surface can therefore", "  return findings seconds/minutes behind the transmitting feed according to the physical profile and", "  declared latency class.", "- **Watermarks close windows from durable coverage, not wall time.** The source watermark is the highest", "  contiguous **epoch-time** range whose expected chunk sequences are sealed or represented by a terminal", "  sequence/capture gap after the profile's timeout. A sealed next sequence with a positive time delta does", "  not bridge missing time; overlap must first record its canonical chunk/range election so duplicate bytes", "  feed no stateful stage. Each stateful stage advances its analysis watermark only after the", "  required attempt markers for that range are terminal under the pinned overload rung. A promotion window", "  closes when its end is behind the analysis watermark by the declared allowed-lateness interval. Explicit", "  epoch close flushes remaining windows at the boundary as complete or partial from recorded coverage.", "  A chunk first arriving after its gap was finalized is always accepted as late evidence. Inside the", "  configured horizon, its bounded late-generation manifest re-enters the same stream-window slot and", "  therefore re-versions/retracts affected outputs rather than minting a parallel event. Outside the", "  horizon, derived outputs remain unchanged until an explicit re-extraction reconstructs the required", "  state.", "- **Promotion waits only for its semantic aggregation window.** Cross-chunk tracks and acoustic/visual", "  detections remain mutable processor state until the window's watermark closes. The live promotion key is", "  stream-scoped\u2014`(stream_epoch_id, promotion_rule_id, epoch-scoped track/member key,", "  aggregation_window_index)`\u2014rather than chunk-scoped. This is an explicit `stream_epoch`-owned promotion", "  slot family in ingestion \u00a73.5/\u00a74.1, backed by the canonical epoch anchor; it is not an item-owned artifact", "  with a missing parent. The promoted event lists exact contribution member addresses from every", "  contributing chunk, and F-ING-10 links all contributing source items. A late reprocessing correction", "  writes a new event version or retraction through the ordinary ingestion \u00a73.5/\u00a74.17 path; it never edits", "  history. An epoch with null `operation_id` routes promotions to the tenant's standing ESS scope. A finer", "  \u00a74.17 serialization key is allowed only when it is part of that event type's declared real-world identity;", "  stream/camera id is not invented as a merge key. Source activation therefore includes expected live", "  promotion rate under the published standing-lane ceiling and DATA-1 sizing.", "- **Clip availability does not delay event identity.** Promotion creates one stable child-evidence request", "  keyed by `(requesting promotion slot or attributed operator request id, clip-policy version, requested", "  epoch-relative range)`. The promotion output transaction creates/references the pending request and", "  carries its labels, operation/destruction epochs, retention basis, and post-roll deadline; retry returns", "  the same row. Coalescing links N stable requests to one deterministic bundle plan. A budget, source-gap,", "  or archive failure resolves the request to an explicit unavailable/skipped outcome. No provisional event", "  identity and no event rewrite are required merely to attach bytes.", "- **A live clip spanning chunks is an ordered bundle, not one multi-parent byte object.** The bundle", "  manifest is keyed by its sealed coalescing-plan identity and lists immutable clip parts in epoch order.", "  Each part remains an ordinary one-parent child object keyed by", "  `(parent source_item_id, child kind=clip, actual chunk-local range, derivation digest)`, inherits that", "  parent's baseline labels, retention, holds, and destruction epochs, and passes quarantine \u2192 evidence", "  promotion independently. Separately sealed plans that resolve to the same key add \u00a79.2 referent rows;", "  effective retention/holds/labels conservatively join all surviving obligations without duplicating bytes.", "  Item/lineage expiry or destruction removes only affected parts and appends their destruction receipts;", "  the bundle persists as a labeled catalog fact with `complete`/`partial`/`destroyed` coverage and never", "  hides a gap. Its bundle-level effective labels are a versioned restrictive join over surviving part", "  records and are recomputed in the same catalog transition when a part is destroyed or relabeled; stale", "  over-restriction is safe but is not accepted as converged state. If no part survives, the catalog stays", "  retracted/destroyed with its last effective labels floored by the epoch anchor\u2014an empty join never becomes", "  unlabeled. An operation-wide hold/destruction", "  naturally reaches every part; an item hold protects only its part. Display may concatenate authorized", "  available parts into a non-evidentiary rendition, while", "  custody exports the ordered part manifest + hashes. Stream-copy/remux and requested-range containment", "  remain \u00a79.2's rules per part.", "", "For a copy source, the cutter first uses already-promoted preceding chunk evidence where it covers pre-roll;", "otherwise it uses a registered customer archive/rewind path. When neither can guarantee the signed window", "(notably epoch start and reference-only feeds), clip-capable activation requires customer sign-off on a", "**tenant-isolated, encrypted, bounded ephemeral rolling packet buffer**. Every packet range is tagged with", "`stream_epoch_id` and may be read/cut only by a request carrying that same epoch, so rebinding never leaks", "new-operation packets into an old clip. Its TTL is at least", "`max_pre_roll + max_post_roll + permitted_processing_lag + cut_finalization_margin` and no longer than the", "signed policy. It is decoder/cutter scratch: not hot-projected, not agent-queryable, not durable raw-video", "evidence, and accessible only through the isolated media worker. A produced clip still passes", "quarantine/validation \u2192 evidence promotion and records the source packet/chunk hashes. Buffer expiry and", "deletion are metered/audited; a clip request that outlives available packets fails explicitly. The buffer", "is a registered non-evidence scratch lifecycle class: every read/cut/delete validates current destruction", "epochs; source-system/stream/epoch destruction or deregistration purges it by deterministic object prefix", "and terminally resolves affected requests unless an", "active legal hold covers an already-requested clip. In that one case, only packets needed for that request", "may survive until the signed bounded finalization deadline; the promoted parts then carry the hold, and the", "raw scratch is purged. A hold never opens new clip requests from old scratch and never preserves the whole", "buffer for its lifetime.", "", "#### 7.7.5 Posture-specific overload\u2014stay honest about live coverage", "", "Load shedding applies when analysis capacity, not byte intake, cannot keep pace. It never silently deletes a", "retained source chunk or cancels already-admitted work. Each source declares ordered, dry-run-tested", "degradation rungs (for example: suppress Tier 2; reduce densification; reduce base sampling within a signed", "minimum; Tier-0/keepalive coverage only). The rung selected when a chunk is planned is pinned in its", "manifest/run identity; skipped stages/ranges become labeled coverage outcomes with reason", "`overload`, not missing rows.", "", "The signed source profile pre-registers compatible ladder variants, their thresholds/hysteresis/dwell, and", "the absolute minimum coverage floor. Operation posture may select one of those bounded variants for the", "epoch; it cannot invent a rung or lower the source floor, and it does not choose the runtime rung. A named", "per-stream-epoch **live overload controller** owns that choice. It reads durable", "`(latest sealed range, analysis watermark, ready/admitted backlog age, active", "rung)` state, changes rung by generation-checked CAS with hysteresis, and records the telemetry snapshot", "and reason. Concurrent planners read one fenced controller version and may apply it only to not-yet-planned", "chunks. Already-planned/admitted entries are immutable obligations.", "", "For live sources, `live_edge_lag` is a third named latency clock alongside ingestion \u00a74.9's", "receipt-rooted clocks: mapped media instant (with its anchor uncertainty) \u2192 finding", "live-query-visible. The physical chunk duration and keyframe wait are structural floors on this clock.", "Controller thresholds and live SLO evidence use it; `received_at \u2192 persisted` alone cannot prove", "instant-to-finding latency.", "", "- **Emergent:** reserve the live critical path and select a declared rung early enough to remain inside the", "  live-edge lag target. Premium enrichment may trail; deterministic/Tier-1 coverage may not fall below the", "  signed minimum without a `coverage_breach` alarm, an explicit uncovered range, and source state", "  `degraded(coverage_floor)`. The capacity controller stops accepting additional commitments on the", "  affected pool and sheds lower-posture unadmitted work first; it never reports the range complete.", "- **Standard:** process at normal depth while lag is below the source's configured bound. At the bound,", "  new chunks use the next declared rung so lag converges rather than growing forever; queued work already", "  admitted completes normally.", "- **Bulk** (archive/backfill use): preserve the configured analysis depth and accept queue latency; it does", "  not claim a live-edge SLO.", "", "The source profile also declares automatic-correction eligibility by stage, replay substrate, maximum cost,", "attempts, duration, and horizon; a zero horizon is valid when no bounded correction can meet the source's", "live SLO. Correction work is a distinct metered work kind admitted under the source's latency lane and", "budgets before it takes the stage fence. The controller includes correction state/age/cost in its durable", "inputs, and any live range degraded while a correction holds the fence records reason", "`late_fill_correction`, not generic overload.", "", "If bytes remain available, an operator may later request re-extraction of degraded ranges under a new", "generation and ordinary bulk admission. That is new measured work, not an automatic mutation that makes the", "original coverage claim disappear. For reference-only sources whose archive/buffer has expired, the", "coverage gap is permanent and queryable.", "", "#### 7.7.6 Live query and activation contract", "", "The \u00a77.6 union accepts a stream/epoch range as well as a single `source_item_id`. It maps each chunk-local", "member through the pinned epoch offset, orders by", "`(stream_id, epoch_sequence, epoch-relative start/end, track rank, complete member address)`, and returns", "sealed chunks only; opaque `stream_epoch_id` never stands in for chronology. At first page, the cursor", "captures a fixed-width revision vector for artifacts/events, canonical coverage artifacts, epoch control, and", "clip request/bundle catalog, plus the last sort key. Every subsequent page evaluates all members and the", "coverage header as of that vector, so chunks sealing or clips resolving mid-scroll neither reorder results", "nor mutate prior header claims. Its coverage header includes expected/sealed chunk ranges, terminal and", "late-filled sequence/capture gaps (including `evidence_only_after_horizon` disposition), capture-overlap", "elections, source discontinuities, analysis", "degradation/uncovered ranges, pending aggregation windows, and pending/partial/unavailable clips.", "Cross-epoch wall-clock queries retain \u00a77.6's confidence", "gate and unplaceable set.", "", "**The revision vector is a causal read receipt, not simultaneous snapshots across databases.** The stream", "control shard maintains an append-versioned stream index of **chunk/stage commit receipts** and", "coverage/clip-state transitions\u2014not one row per artifact member. A receipt names the sealed chunk/range,", "stage-manifest digest, address-index key, authority revision interval, and causal predecessor; the", "authoritative SoR index enumerates member addresses under that committed manifest. This keeps control write", "rate proportional to chunks/stages rather than sampled frames or findings. Receipts are time-partitioned;", "once below every active cursor and correction/replay horizon, contiguous ranges compact to immutable", "summary roots + archive pointers under the source coverage policy. Thus a multi-day epoch does not require", "an unbounded hot control table or forced product-visible rotation.", "", "SoR artifact/event commits and retained clip-part catalog commits each have a monotonic logical authority", "revision plus a **committed low watermark**: the highest revision below which no transaction remains open.", "Ordinary assigned-sequence maxima are never snapshot boundaries. Physical shard LSNs are not cursor fields.", "At page one, the query coordinator freezes a control-index revision, derives the registered authority", "intervals reachable from its exact chunk/stage receipts, and waits until each authority's committed low", "watermark covers them. It then issues a snapshot lease containing the fixed vector", "`(control_revision, artifact_revision, evidence_catalog_revision)`, last sort key, and expiry. Unrelayed", "output-first commits are deliberately absent until their receipt registers; this preserves causal closure", "without 2PC.", "", "Each authority supports address-filtered as-of reads and retains append-only state history for at least the", "maximum cursor TTL; mutable epoch/watermark/request/catalog rows version rather than erase prior read state.", "Compaction may prune only below both the minimum active snapshot revision and the TTL floor. The lease pins", "metadata history, not destroyed evidence bytes. Every page still revalidates current authorization, labels,", "and destruction epochs; a security/destruction change invalidates the token instead of mutating an earlier", "coverage claim, resurrecting bytes, or widening access. An expired/invalidated token returns an explicit", "restart requirement. Activation/load evidence must prove receipt repair, low-watermark correctness,", "history retention/compaction, causal-cut construction, and token expiry across all three authorities.", "", "Activation fails unless the source entry declares and the dry-run proves: transport/codec + keyframe", "behavior; physical profile bounds; discontinuity/reconnect handling; operation binding; clock-anchor", "quality, timestamp unwrap, per-track offsets, and A/V drift; archive rewind or signed", "ephemeral-buffer/replay-substrate policy; evidence retention; aggregation/clip windows;", "gap timeout/allowed lateness plus the late-processing horizon; checkpoint/warm-up retention and parent-byte", "processing availability through the maximum declared bound; overload rungs, lag targets, hysteresis, and", "minimum coverage; and source behavior when Polaris applies backpressure. Conformance/load tests cover", "competing segmenters and stale", "epoch generations; takeover/reshard during active sealing; lost/duplicated/out-of-order/late-filled chunks;", "hash mismatch; timestamp wrap/reset, capture gaps/overlaps, and per-track drift;", "watermark/gap/epoch-close flushing; cross-chunk tracks/transcripts/promotions/clip bundles; crash at", "every checkpoint/output/relay/CAS boundary; buffer expiry, destruction, deregistration, and bounded", "hold-finalization; standard-lag transition and concurrent planners; emergent floor breach;", "control/chunk admission-shadow failover/receipt repair; correction-generation identity, deadline", "abandonment/fence release, and late fill inside/outside its horizon; replay/re-extraction; stream destruction", "including orphan scratch; part-referent hold/destruction and bundle-label recomputation; committed revision", "low-watermark gaps; and deterministic union pagination while chunks seal and clip requests resolve.", "", "## 8. Chunk plan", "", "| Chunk | Covers | Status |", "|---|---|---|", "| Skeleton (this) | Scope, settled inputs, processing model outline, forks | **DONE 2026-07-19** |", "| Image pipeline | Vision extraction targets by context, detection/OCR artifact shapes, entity-observation + event promotion | **DONE 2026-07-20 (\u00a75)** \u2014 M-4/M-5/M-6 resolved |", "| Audio pipeline | Transcript pipeline (diarization, non-speech description), artifact shape per M-2, promotion-to-events config | **DONE 2026-07-20 (\u00a76)** \u2014 M-5/M-6 resolved |", "| Video pipeline | Frame-sampling mechanics (rates by context), dual-track orchestration, long-running/live streams, M-1 evaluation design (execution/results open) | **DESIGN DONE; BUILD PHASED** \u2014 finite-video design authored 2026-07-20; union read contract (\u00a77.6) authored 2026-07-21; \u00a77.7 live-stream build is deferred/need-triggered per its phasing block; M-1 eval execution gated on footage corpus |", "| Storage & clip policy | Clip windows/defaults (M-3), external-reference validation/acquisition, retained-volume model, per-source sign-off flow | **DONE 2026-07-21 (\u00a79)** \u2014 byte classes, clip mechanics (stream-copy cut, coalescing, caps), reference liveness, volume model, fail-closed sign-off (no default retention duration) |", "| GovCloud serving | In-boundary serving matrix (vision + audio), GPU floor, in-VPC screening criteria, cost-model shape, in-account runbook | **AUTHORED 2026-07-21 (\u00a710)** \u2014 design complete; GPU families verified in-region in both gov regions (no G5/G6e/Inf2 \u2014 L4-class memory constraint on in-VPC VLMs; workload fit unverified pre-eval); the \u00a710.5 in-account runbook closes the open numbers and feeds M-1 eval execution |", "", "## 9. Storage & clip policy (authored 2026-07-21)", "", "What this chunk fixes: the **retained-byte model** for media sources \u2014 which bytes Polaris durably keeps,", "how evidence clips are cut, identified, and retained (M-3 made concrete), how external-reference sources", "are validated over time, the arithmetic that makes retained volume a config decision instead of a surprise,", "and the customer sign-off flow the program requires (FR-4.2/4.4; OD-3; STATE 2026-07-14). Nothing here", "re-decides the settled inputs (\u00a72): clips + analysis may be the retained evidence for external-reference", "sources even when the original is not; retention is per-source-type config set at onboarding with customer", "sign-off.", "", "### 9.1 The byte classes (what is durably retained, and why)", "", "| Byte class | Origin | Retention driver |", "|---|---|---|", "| Promoted source payloads (copy sources) | quarantine \u2192 evidence lake (ingestion \u00a73.0) | per-source OD-3 policy |", "| External-reference receipt | **no source bytes at acceptance** \u2014 the canonical row carries a usable versioned reference and permitted hash/archive metadata (FR-4.4) | n/a for the receipt; \u00a79.3 governs later acquisitions |", "| **Evidence clips** | promotion-driven child objects (\u00a75.4, \u00a79.2) | clip policy \u2014 **the dominant retained volume** (STATE 2026-07-14) |", "| Retained analyzed frames / stills | `evidence` config block (\u00a75.6) | per-source policy |", "| Audio extracts | child objects (\u00a77.2) | per-source policy |", "| Acquired external original | controlled dereference \u2192 immutable intent, fenced work state, immutable terminal result; quarantine while untrusted, then scanned-transient staging or durable promotion only for a successful fetch | per-source OD-3 policy for metadata/verdict; partial bytes remain quarantined and are destroyed; transient bytes are destroyed when all referencing manifest entries are terminal; durable bytes follow the source retention stanza |", "| Live correction replay substrate (only when automatic late correction is enabled) | promoted chunks, customer rewind, retained deterministic intermediates, or signed encrypted scratch | gap timeout + late horizon + replay/finalization margin; scratch is non-evidence and destruction-fenced |", "| Operational coverage + manifest facts | intake ledger (ingestion \u00a74.1) | prunable after terminal state plus the declared replay floor |", "| Agent-facing semantic/frame coverage | Accelerate coverage row or versioned `media_analysis_coverage` artifact | follows the source item's evidence/retention policy; authoritative input to hot projection |", "", "The initial posture for external-reference sources, stated once: **the referenced original is not retained", "evidence merely because its receipt was accepted.** What Polaris stands behind evidentially is what it actually", "acquired and retained\u2014potentially the original under `durable_allowed`, plus clips, frames, and analysis", "artifacts, and canonical coverage artifacts, all hash-addressed and labeled. If the customer's archive ages out (CCTV loop", "recording measures retention in days), reprocessing under new model generations becomes impossible for ranges", "that have no durable acquisition or other retained replay substrate \u2014 analysis and clips stand, coverage records what was processed at which generation, and", "the limitation is declared at sign-off (\u00a79.5), never discovered in an incident.", "Ordinary cross-chunk analysis still processes a live reference feed as packets arrive. Automatic correction", "of a late gap is separately capability-gated: each stage declares whether it can reconstruct from retained", "deterministic intermediates, customer rewind, promoted chunk evidence, or a signed bounded local replay", "cache. Without one, that source/stage uses horizon zero and the late arrival remains evidence-only.", "", "### 9.2 Clip mechanics (M-3 made concrete)", "", "- **Trigger \u2014 settled, restated:** clip requests ride **event promotion** (\u00a75.4); the promotion config's", "  per-class policy gains a `clip` flag (promote-with-clip / promote-only). Operator- or consumer-requested", "  clips (an investigator marking a range) enter the same machinery as explicit requests through the", "  platform API \u2014 same identity, same path; the request surface itself is downstream (Apollo PRD).", "- **Window \u2014 track-scoped:** the requested window is the promoting **track's interval** expanded by", "  per-class pre/post margins (config; \u00a79.5 seeds). Standalone images and `evidence_video`/`evidence_photo`", "  sources need no clips \u2014 the promoted payload is already retained whole (copy sources).", "- **Coalescing \u2014 within a sealed plan, never across time (2026-07-21, pass-4):** overlapping or", "  near-adjacent requested windows (gap below a config threshold) merge into **one clip object for a finite", "  parent, or one ordered clip-bundle plan for a live stream**, but only", "  among the requests known when the **clip plan seals** \u2014 it seals with its generation's budget window,", "  exactly like densification (ingestion \u00a74.1) \u2014 so the coalescing cluster, and therefore the merged actual", "  range/part plan, is deterministic over a closed request set. Each promoting event references the shared", "  clip or bundle plus its own sub-range; bytes are stored once *within a sealed cluster*. **Late requests**", "  (post-seal promotions, investigator marks): if an existing clip's actual range covers the requested", "  window, reference it; otherwise mint a **new clip/bundle plan under its own key** \u2014 overlap between", "  separately-sealed plans is tolerated. An existing clip/part is **never widened, rewritten, or re-keyed**", "  (immutable evidence, \u00a77.2). For live streams, the aggregation/clip watermark seals a bounded request set", "  while the epoch continues; it never waits for stream completion (\u00a77.7.4).", "- **Caps:** per-item and per-hour **clip-seconds budgets** per source (the \u00a75.6 budget pattern). Over-cap", "  clip requests are recorded `skipped(budget)` in the manifest (operator alarm \u2014 a cap collision on an", "  evidence path is a sign-off-values problem, not a silent drop); the promoted event itself is unaffected.", "- **Cutting \u2014 stream-copy, never re-encode (wording sharpened 2026-07-21, pass-4):** clips are", "  container-level **stream copies \u2014 no elementary-stream re-encoding**: the encoded video/audio packets are", "  the original's, cut at the enclosing keyframe/GOP boundaries and **remuxed** into a new container", "  (container headers, index, and timestamps are necessarily new \u2014 the clip is *derived from* the accepted", "  original, not byte-identical to a slice of it, and custody presentation claims exactly that: **provable", "  derivation, never byte identity**). The derivation is fully recorded on the child-evidence record: source", "  five-part object reference, requested + actual ranges, cutter + muxer versions/config, output hash. The requested", "  window is always **contained in** the actual range. Rationale: the evidentiary content is the customer's", "  original encoded stream \u2014 a transcode is Polaris-generated imagery with generation loss and codec choices", "  we would then have to defend. Display renditions (normalized codecs for browser playback) are derived", "  display objects, generated downstream on demand (Apollo PRD) and never the evidence object. The cut is", "  deterministic given (container bytes, cutter + muxer version) \u2014 it rides \u00a77.2's child identity", "  (derivation digest) unchanged. For a live bundle, these rules apply independently to each parent-owned", "  part; the ordered manifest\u2014not a byte rewrite\u2014joins them. Audio-only clips are segment extracts under", "  the same rules.", "- **Identity, lifecycle, labels:** clips are **child evidence objects**, not \u00a73.5 artifacts \u2014 no artifact", "  row, no supersession (the \u00a75.4 rule: never retracted). Every byte object has exactly one parent and key =", "  (parent item, `clip`, canonical locator of the **actual** parent-local range, derivation digest);", "  quarantine \u2192 promote; manifest-tracked byte state; addressed by its full five-part object reference; labels,", "  retention, holds, and destruction epochs inherit from that parent (ingestion \u00a74.1 child rule). A", "  cross-chunk live clip is the \u00a77.7.4 **logical bundle** of these ordinary objects: its labeled manifest", "  carries requested/actual epoch ranges, ordered part five-part references, per-part coverage/status, referencing", "  requests/events, and a restrictive effective-label join for bundle-level discovery. It contains no", "  shared bytes and never weakens per-part authorization. Two separately sealed plans may legitimately", "  resolve to the same canonical part key/range; each adds an immutable **part-referent row** carrying its", "  bundle/request, policy/retention basis, labels, hold, and lifecycle. The byte object is still stored once.", "  Its effective `retain_until` is the maximum source baseline/live-referent deadline, holds are the union,", "  and labels are the restrictive join over parent + live referents. Removing one referent cannot delete or", "  relax a part still required by another; ordinary expiry destroys only after no surviving obligation", "  remains. Authorized parent/scope destruction still wins subject to the existing legal-hold rule.", "  **The child-evidence record is a retained evidence fact, never prunable", "  operational state (2026-07-21, pass-4):** ingestion \u00a74.1's retention split classifies it with coverage", "  rows \u2014 each part's durable record (parent/stream epoch/operation identity, requested + actual ranges,", "  five-part object reference, labels, cutter/derivation identity, referent rows and effective **policy/retention/hold", "  projection**, destruction state + receipt) persists per the source's policy and is", "  what serves \"all clips for this item/operation\"; the bundle catalog persists its ordered status/history.", "  Enumeration never depends on prunable operational manifest state.", "- **Never retracted \u2260 never destroyed (2026-07-21, pass-4):** supersession never removes a clip, but", "  OD-3/DATA-7 destruction does \u2014 retention expiry, client offboarding, operation-scoped destruction", "  (FR-4.9). An executed destruction replaces each affected part's bytes with a **destruction record**", "  (when, under which policy version, by whose authority, receipt) on that child-evidence record and updates", "  every bundle that references it to `partial` or `destroyed`. Unaffected parts survive; a read surfaces the", "  ordered gap + destruction record \u2014 never a dead pointer, never silence.", "", "### 9.3 External-reference validation and acquisition (the \u00a73.0 dereference contract)", "", "- **At onboarding, per source:** archive locator scheme + auth material; reference resolution exercised on", "  samples; **hash acquisition method declared** \u2014 customer-supplied manifest hashes vs computed on first", "  full read (a full read of huge objects is a real cost \u2014 declared, not assumed); the archive's **retention", "  window and mutation behavior declared** (loop-recording overwrite, WORM, versioning) and recorded on the", "  authoritative immutable `ingest_control` source-policy version\u2014never a ledger policy mirror. This is the", "  \u00a79.1 posture's input, and the ledger work pins its policy id/version/digest.", "- **In operation:** every permitted acquisition verifies the expected hash/version when the source provides", "  one (mismatch = terminal-fail + alarm, never silent) and records the acquired hash regardless. Added here:", "  a per-source **reference liveness probe**. A metadata-only reachability/version probe may run for every", "  policy without reading object bytes and records no scan/acquisition claim. A hash probe reads bytes, is a", "  `TRANSIENT` acquisition with purpose `reference_liveness_probe`, and may run only when", "  `dereference_policy` permits fetching. Its deterministic generation is the versioned probe schedule id +", "  scheduled window; it streams the hash without decode or staging, records explicitly `hash_only` with no", "  malware-scan verdict, and discards bytes as the stream completes. Both probe forms are sampled and", "  scheduled on a configured cadence; both append a tenant-scoped DataLake2 ledger liveness check and update", "  its derived current state, so archive drift surfaces operationally instead of at the next", "  reprocessing attempt. A degraded reference (unreachable, hash", "  mismatch, aged out) marks the DataLake2 ledger liveness row\u2014not the canonical Accelerate receipt\u2014", "  `degraded(reason, since)`: committed analysis and clips stand", "  (they are the retained evidence); new processing against the reference is blocked; nothing is retracted.", "- **Dereference policy:** `prohibited`, `transient_only`, or `durable_allowed`. Fetching is never implied by", "  accepting the reference. Every authorized attempt commits an immutable intent before I/O and one immutable", "  terminal result after I/O; fenced lease/retry state is separate. A successful result records exact", "  source/object identity, scan/structural verdict, and transient or durable disposition. No-byte and failed", "  results have no scan claim; partial bytes stay quarantined and are destroyed. A durable acquisition may", "  retain the original; transient acquisition deletes it after permitted processing while keeping audit", "  metadata and its destruction receipt.", "", "### 9.4 The retained-volume model (arithmetic \u2014 assumptions labeled)", "", "Clip volume per source class is a four-knob product, all four knobs per-source config:", "", "```", "retained clip bytes/day \u2248 H \u00d7 a \u00d7 c \u00d7 w\u0304 \u00d7 r", "  H = camera-hours/day    a = active fraction (Tier-0)    c = coalesced CLIP OBJECTS/PARTS per active hour", "  w\u0304 = mean STORED object/part seconds (actual range: window + track + keyframe expansion)    r = bytes/s", "steady-state \u2248 daily rate \u00d7 retention days", "```", "", "Live automatic correction adds a bounded **scratch-capacity**, not retained-evidence, term:", "", "```", "peak replay-substrate bytes \u2248 active streams \u00d7 replay-substrate bytes/s", "                              \u00d7 (gap timeout + late horizon + replay/finalization margin)", "```", "", "For promoted copy chunks that capacity is already counted in source-payload retention; for customer rewind", "it is an external archive dependency; for retained deterministic intermediates the dry-run substitutes", "their measured byte rate. A raw local replay cache is permitted only as signed, destruction-fenced scratch", "and must appear explicitly in the capacity/sign-off report.", "", "The unit is the **stored clip object/part**, not the promoting event or metadata-only live bundle \u2014", "multiplying *promotions* by a shared post-coalescing duration would count the same bytes once per", "referencing event (2026-07-21, pass-4);", "duration is the **actual stored range** (keyframe expansion included), and `r` should be the source's", "*measured* byte rate for variable-bitrate footage \u2014 the dry-run computes both from real samples. Worked", "example (assumptions: 1080p H.264 CCTV \u2248 3 Mbps \u2248 1.4 GB/hour; `cctv_fixed` defaults; **no-overlap", "estimate** \u2014 clips assumed non-coalescing, so coalescing only shrinks it): 100 cameras", "\u00d7 24 h = 2,400 camera-hours/day; a = 0.1; c = 2; w\u0304 = 40 s \u2192 ~19,200 clip-seconds/day \u2248 **~7 GB/day**, \u2248", "**5 TB steady-state at 2-year retention**. Same formula at the extreme tier (petabyte-class/hour \u2248 high", "hundreds of thousands of camera-hours/hour at that bitrate) yields **~2 TB/hour of clips** \u2014 consistent", "with the STATE 2026-07-14 ~TB/hour figure and the reason this chunk exists. Ranked levers, steepest first:", "**retention duration** (linear, unbounded), **promotion-with-clip density** (p \u2014 per-class policy),", "**window size** (w), **caps** (the \u00a79.2 backstop). Transcripts, detections, and coverage rows are", "noise-level next to clip bytes (single-digit-% derived-output ratio, STATE 2026-07-14). The onboarding", "dry-run report (FR-2.4) computes this projection from the source's actual sample footage \u2014 the sign-off", "below is taken against those numbers, not against defaults.", "", "### 9.5 Per-source sign-off flow (FR-4.2/4.4 made procedural)", "", "Clip + retention policy is part of the authoritative immutable DATA-12 ingestion source policy in", "`ingest_control`, so the flow **is** the FR-2.3/2.4", "onboarding flow with an explicit evidence-policy stanza:", "", "1. **Propose:** context-class defaults seed the policy \u2014 margins (order: pre 10 s / post 10 s), max clip", "   length (order: 120 s), coalescing gap (order: 5 s), per-class clip flags, caps. Order-of-magnitude", "   seeds, dry-run-validated \u2014 the \u00a77.3 pattern.", "2. **Dry-run** (FR-2.4): sample footage end-to-end; report shows projected retained volume (\u00a79.4), spend,", "   example clips, replay-substrate peak capacity, and coverage \u2014 what would be kept, what would be dropped,", "   what it costs.", "3. **Sign off \u2014 recorded, fail-closed:** the customer's sign-off (actor, timestamp, policy version \u2014 the", "   FR-2.3 record) asserts: what may be **dropped** (funnel/skip rules \u2014 the STATE open-question-1", "   obligation), what is **clipped**, how long everything is **retained**, the **archive-dependency", "   acknowledgment** for external-reference sources (\u00a79.1 posture + \u00a79.3 declared archive characteristics), any", "   live-source ephemeral rolling-buffer bounds/access/TTL plus the maximum hold-finalization extension for", "   already-requested clips (\u00a77.7.4), the live late-processing horizon plus checkpoint/warm-up and parent", "   processing-availability/archive/replay-substrate bound (including horizon zero where correction is", "   unsupported), the ordered-part/gap behavior for cross-chunk clips, and the", "   destruction-authority pointer (DATA-7, FR-4.9). **Retention duration has no platform default**: it is a", "   required sign-off value per byte class, and activation fails without it. Polaris records, enforces, and", "   evidences the customer's retention decision \u2014 it never presumes one (jurisdictional evidence-retention", "   rules are the customer's to assert).", "4. **Change = re-version + re-sign:** policy edits follow FR-2.3 versioning; a retention shortening is a", "   destruction-adjacent act and rides DATA-7's evidence rules, never a silent config edit. Transition", "   mechanics: ingestion \u00a74.12 (pass-5, 2026-07-22) \u2014 policy changes are prospective by default; a", "   retrospective shortening is an attributed, hold-checked transition job through the destruction", "   machinery, with the old basis preserved in history and destruction evidence produced.", "", "## 10. GovCloud serving (authored 2026-07-21)", "", "What this chunk fixes: **where each tier's models run, per boundary** \u2014 the serving matrix, the verified", "GPU floor, the screening criteria for in-VPC candidates, the cost-model shape, and the consolidated", "in-account runbook that closes the open numbers. It feeds M-1 eval execution (\u00a77.4 needs the in-boundary", "price/quota axis). Nothing here re-decides the settled posture: in-VPC CV at firehose scale, text", "extraction on Bedrock, frame sampling as the committed visual baseline (\u00a72).", "", "### 10.1 The serving matrix (capability \u00d7 boundary)", "", "| Capability | Commercial | GovCloud (ENV-1 / ENV-5-on-AWS) | Non-AWS / air-gapped ENV-5 | Gate |", "|---|---|---|---|---|", "| Tier 0 \u2014 decode, segmentation, VAD, EXIF, hashes | CPU on EKS | CPU on EKS | CPU on EKS | none (codec/tooling licenses ride \u00a710.3 screening) |", "| Tier 1 \u2014 CV detect/track/plate-read | in-VPC GPU on EKS | in-VPC GPU on EKS (**committed** \u2014 STATE 2026-07-14) | in-VPC GPU | GPU floor verified (\u00a710.2); account quotas in-account (\u00a710.5) |", "| Tier 2 \u2014 OCR | hosted or in-VPC engine | in-VPC engine (hosted only if authorized) | in-VPC engine | \u00a710.3 screening |", "| Tier 2 \u2014 VLM on frames | hosted VLM | **candidate: authorized Claude on Bedrock frames** (exact dated allowlist \u2014 \u00a72; a candidate, not the selected path, until \u00a710.5 items 1\u20132 pass); in-VPC open VLM as the other candidate | in-VPC open VLM only | **image input on gov endpoints + effective model access \u2014 in-account (\u00a710.5)**; in-VPC candidates face the \u00a710.2 memory constraint |", "| Native video | Nova (per M-1 eval, per-source) | **none until Nova FedRAMP lands** (verified absent 2026-07-20 \u2014 watch) | none (no in-VPC native-video assumption) | authorization watch item |", "| ASR + diarization | managed or in-VPC | **Transcribe** (in-region + authorized, verified 2026-07-20; Call Analytics unavailable; language-ID/redaction west-only) vs in-VPC ASR | **in-VPC ASR required** | quality eval (\u00a710.4 note); feature set in-account |", "| AED (acoustic events) | in-VPC model | in-VPC model | in-VPC model | not a Transcribe feature (2026-07-20 posture); \u00a710.3 screening |", "", "**The air-gapped column is a future compatibility target, not day-one build scope (corrected 2026-07-21,", "pass-4** \u2014 build-for-the-tier-sold, STATE 2026-07-14; the same posture F-ING-8 applies to Strimzi): no", "non-AWS boundary is sold, so nothing in this chunk commits an offline ASR or VLM stack now. ENV-1 /", "ENV-5-on-AWS picks are made on their own merits \u2014 managed vs in-VPC compared on quality, features, cost,", "and ops burden by the serving eval. **AED is the one in-VPC commitment regardless of boundary**, because no", "managed AED path is claimed (the 2026-07-20 posture). If universal offline serving ever becomes committed", "scope, that is an explicit program decision, not an inference inside this chunk.", "Embeddings are noted for completeness only \u2014 Titan V2 / Titan Multimodal G1 are authorized (STATE", "2026-07-10) and ride the ENV-3 / FR-3.8 per-deployment config, not this chunk.", "", "### 10.2 The verified GPU floor (2026-07-21 \u2014 AWS EC2 instance-types-by-Region documentation)", "", "Accelerated-computing families listed per region (source: AWS EC2 \"instance types by Region\" docs page,", "fetched 2026-07-21; G6 = NVIDIA L4 per the AWS G6-in-GovCloud launch announcement, 2024-11):", "", "- **us-gov-west-1** (primary): G4dn (T4-class), **G6 / Gr6 (L4-class)**, Inf1, P3dn, **P4d, P5, P5en,", "  P6-B200**, plus legacy F1/G3/P2/P3.", "- **us-gov-east-1**: G4dn, **G6 / Gr6**, Inf1, P3dn, P6-B300.", "", "Reading for this workload (evidence level kept honest \u2014 2026-07-21, pass-4): **candidate inference-class", "hardware is listed in-region in both GovCloud regions** \u2014 the *availability* half of the 2026-07-14", "\"GovCloud GPU capacity/quotas\" must-verify closes at the **family-listing level** (as-of 2026-07-21; the", "EC2 page itself notes regional support need not mean every Availability Zone). **Workload fit stays", "UNVERIFIED until the \u00a710.3 screening + serving eval measure a real candidate** \u2014 model memory after runtime", "overhead, throughput, driver/device-plugin support on EKS, quota, obtainable capacity, cost; family listing", "is not feasibility. Equally load-bearing is", "what is **absent** (an inference from the current region list, same as-of date): no G5 (A10G), no G6e", "(L40S-class), no Inf2 \u2014 the mid-size GPU tier does not appear in", "GovCloud, so an in-VPC open-VLM candidate must **fit L4-class memory (24 GB, quantization included)** or", "jump straight to P4d/P5 training-class economics. That is a \u00a710.3 screening constraint, not a blocker: the", "committed Tier-1 CV workload (detectors, trackers, plate/OCR models) *targets* the G4dn/G6 class \u2014 typical", "footprints run far below 24 GB, an expectation the screening confirms per candidate, not a verified fact. Placement: Karpenter GPU node pools on the datalake EKS cluster (ingestion F-ING-8), scaling", "with the extraction worker tier on SQS depth; fleet sizing stays DATA-1-gated like all capacity planning.", "", "### 10.3 Screening criteria for in-VPC candidates (Tier 1/2 vision, ASR, AED \u2014 the \u00a75.1 rule made concrete)", "", "No candidate model is named-and-endorsed here; candidates are screened on these criteria, then quality is", "decided by the eval \u2014 never asserted from reputation:", "", "1. **License class:** permissive (Apache/MIT-class) preferred; copyleft (AGPL-class) **flagged** \u2014 shipping", "   into a customer boundary (ENV-5) triggers obligations that need legal review; weights-redistribution", "   rights reviewed explicitly (ENV-6 packages what we ship). Every candidate's license is verified at", "   screening, never assumed.", "2. **Offline operation:** no telemetry, no phone-home, no license-server egress \u2014 boundary rule; verified", "   by inspection, not vendor claim.", "3. **GPU footprint:** fits the \u00a710.2 floor (L4-class 24 GB, quantization documented) or carries an explicit", "   P-family cost justification.", "4. **Determinism:** reproducible at fixed weights/config \u2014 the \u00a75.3 `run_id` posture (bitwise GPU", "   determinism not claimed). A live stateful stage may use \u00a77.7.1's early correction convergence only when", "   its canonical plaintext state/output digests prove the stronger reproducibility; otherwise correction", "   runs to the captured frontier.", "5. **Provenance & maintenance:** weights provenance stated; active maintenance; SBOM-able packaging", "   (ENV-6).", "", "### 10.4 Cost-model shape (structure now; numbers from the eval + in-account)", "", "The unit is **GPU-hours (or hosted-model dollars) per camera-hour, per tier, at a context's sampling", "config**: Tier-1 cost scales with sampled frames/s \u00d7 per-frame inference time; Tier-2 with flagged-frame", "rate \u00d7 per-call cost (hosted: tokens; in-VPC: GPU-time); ASR with speech-hours (post-VAD, the Tier-0", "funnel's win). The M-1 eval already scores cost/hour per arm (\u00a77.4) \u2014 this chunk adds the in-boundary", "price axis once in-account rates land (gov rates typically run above commercial \u2014 the standing", "program note). **No throughput or quality numbers are asserted pre-eval**; the \u00a710.5 runbook plus the", "eval's measured yield-per-dollar produce them.", "", "### 10.5 The in-account runbook (what closes this chunk's open numbers)", "", "| # | Check | How | Unblocks |", "|---|---|---|---|", "| 1 | **Claude image input on gov endpoints** | one Bedrock invoke with an image against an authorized Claude model in us-gov-west-1 | the in-boundary hosted-VLM arm (\u00a710.1, \u00a77.4) |", "| 2 | Effective authorized Claude set | console model-access list vs the two public pages (they disagree \u2014 STATE 2026-07-10) | which Claude tiers the mix may use |", "| 3 | Bedrock TPM/RPM quotas for that set | Service Quotas console | hosted-arm scale ceiling; M-1 quota analysis |", "| 4 | GPU Service Quotas (G4dn / G6 / Gr6; P4d/P5 only if VLM self-hosting is pursued) | Service Quotas console (G/P vCPU quotas often default to 0) | Tier-1 fleet capacity planning |", "| 5 | Transcribe effective feature set in us-gov-west-1 | console/API probe (diarization, custom vocabulary, languages; language-ID + redaction are west-only per 2026-07-20 verify) | the ASR pick's managed arm |", "| 6 | Gov pricing pulls \u2014 Bedrock rates, GPU instance rates | pricing pages / in-account | the \u00a710.4 price axis; commercial run-rate input |", "| 7 | **Standing watch:** Nova on the Bedrock FedRAMP page | recheck on a cadence | the native-video in-boundary arm |", "| 8 | Sustained live decode + Tier-1 rate at signed coverage floor | soak registered stream mixes on target EKS/GPU families, including node/AZ loss | continuous-live activation capacity and reserved-floor formula |", "| 9 | Live copied-chunk validation/malware gate | measure configured scanner/decoder-isolation paths at chunk byte/rate profiles | true media-instant latency floor and CPU fleet size |", "| 10 | KEDA/Karpenter reserved-live behavior | scale from floor, saturate, recover, and observe admission rejection/degraded coverage | emergent live capacity evidence |", "| 11 | S3/MinIO conditional create at live cadence | concurrent same/different-hash chunk and checkpoint writes under retry | child/checkpoint idempotency and object-store ceiling |", "| 12 | Control/admission + causal-receipt throughput | exercise chunk/stage receipts, shadows, committed low watermarks, and reshard | DATA-1 control-plane ceiling and SA topology validation |"], "blocks": [{"start": 1, "end": 10, "label": "Design \u2014 Media Processing & Storage (images / audio / video)"}, {"start": 11, "end": 22, "label": "1. Scope & why now"}, {"start": 23, "end": 54, "label": "2. Settled inputs (program decisions \u2014 do not re-decide)"}, {"start": 55, "end": 80, "label": "3. Processing model per modality (to be authored in chunks)"}, {"start": 81, "end": 247, "label": "4. Open forks & verify items"}, {"start": 248, "end": 444, "label": "5. Image pipeline (authored 2026-07-20)"}, {"start": 445, "end": 513, "label": "6. Audio pipeline (authored 2026-07-20 \u2014 M-2 fixed the shape; this chunk fills mechanics, schema, pr"}, {"start": 514, "end": 1159, "label": "7. Video pipeline (authored 2026-07-20)"}, {"start": 1160, "end": 1170, "label": "8. Chunk plan"}, {"start": 1171, "end": 1374, "label": "9. Storage & clip policy (authored 2026-07-21)"}, {"start": 1375, "end": 1474, "label": "10. GovCloud serving (authored 2026-07-21)"}], "lineCount": 1474, "sha256": "68e03b51a655107264377591ff9d4f1aa825cd83c03dd691310dd00d363cc4ba", "endsWithNewline": true});
